1
00:00:05,790 --> 00:00:07,630
♫Turtle, turtle, turtle♫

2
00:00:07,660 --> 00:00:09,680
♫Turtle, turtle, turtle♫

3
00:00:09,700 --> 00:00:11,330
♫Turtles have four legs♫

4
00:00:11,350 --> 00:00:12,970
♫Four feet walking along♫

5
00:00:12,990 --> 00:00:14,900
♫Popping its head in and out♫

6
00:00:14,930 --> 00:00:15,610
What's wrong, Grandpa?

7
00:00:16,430 --> 00:00:18,560
Has the turtle shell been preventing
blood flow to your brain?

8
00:00:18,720 --> 00:00:21,210
I'm trying to act cute

9
00:00:21,230 --> 00:00:23,010
so you will stop being mad at me.

10
00:00:23,030 --> 00:00:24,770
Are you still mad at me?

11
00:00:27,330 --> 00:00:28,030
Whatever.

12
00:00:28,380 --> 00:00:30,320
I will handle what I did

13
00:00:31,410 --> 00:00:32,890
to your mother myself.

14
00:00:33,250 --> 00:00:36,410
But can we deal with
Gaysorn's situation first?

15
00:00:36,550 --> 00:00:37,910
You’d better keep your word,

16
00:00:38,190 --> 00:00:39,530
or you'll end up with an even uglier costume.

17
00:00:40,890 --> 00:00:41,560
Fine.

18
00:00:41,900 --> 00:00:43,370
Where have you been?

19
00:00:43,530 --> 00:00:44,730
Hey, what is that envelope?

20
00:00:45,970 --> 00:00:47,900
I signed a property purchase agreement
with Mr. Sompong.

21
00:00:49,750 --> 00:00:51,320
What, Grandpa?

22
00:00:52,010 --> 00:00:54,160
Of course I'll help you find
Grandma Gaysorn.

23
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:55,750
We still have two months left.

24
00:00:56,090 --> 00:00:57,190
We'll find her.

25
00:00:58,370 --> 00:01:00,350
Do you have any keepsakes

26
00:01:00,370 --> 00:01:02,280
that might be connected to Grandma Gaysorn?

27
00:01:02,300 --> 00:01:03,250
No, I do not.

28
00:01:03,360 --> 00:01:05,580
Your granny was insanely jealous.

29
00:01:05,600 --> 00:01:06,710
One day,

30
00:01:06,910 --> 00:01:10,880
she found out I had
a jade ring that matched Gaysorn's.

31
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:12,460
She snatched it

32
00:01:12,480 --> 00:01:15,010
and crushed it as if it were a rice cracker!

33
00:01:15,030 --> 00:01:15,920
Whoa...

34
00:01:16,390 --> 00:01:17,250
Granny was very scary, huh?

35
00:01:17,270 --> 00:01:18,220
She was!

36
00:01:20,750 --> 00:01:21,250
Mm.

37
00:01:26,160 --> 00:01:27,500
Oh, hey!

38
00:01:28,240 --> 00:01:29,630
Why did you bang your head
against the door?

39
00:01:29,650 --> 00:01:30,160
Hey,

40
00:01:30,390 --> 00:01:31,870
you don't have to knock at this point.

41
00:01:31,890 --> 00:01:33,270
I knocked to let you know
I was coming in.

42
00:01:33,289 --> 00:01:36,039
I can't imagine opening the door
and seeing your little eggies on display.

43
00:01:36,960 --> 00:01:39,150
Can you stop saying "little eggy" already?

44
00:01:39,170 --> 00:01:40,950
You said it so much that
Duidui started mocking me,

45
00:01:40,970 --> 00:01:42,470
"Little Eggy, Little Eggy."

46
00:01:42,490 --> 00:01:44,070
Everyone in this dorm calls me that now.

47
00:01:44,090 --> 00:01:45,130
Ugh, stop talking already.

48
00:01:45,150 --> 00:01:46,500
I have some news for you.

49
00:01:46,520 --> 00:01:47,070
Yeah?

50
00:01:47,090 --> 00:01:50,300
There's a tenant who said
he's Grandma Gaysorn's relative!

51
00:01:53,900 --> 00:01:54,350
Really?

52
00:01:54,370 --> 00:01:55,100
Yeah!

53
00:01:55,240 --> 00:01:57,250
Little Eggy, you're happy, huh?

54
00:02:00,610 --> 00:02:01,890
Little Eggy.

55
00:02:05,900 --> 00:02:06,830
I will finally get to meet her...

56
00:02:08,470 --> 00:02:09,479
Why are you acting so nonchalant?

57
00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:10,330
Aren't you happy?

58
00:02:10,699 --> 00:02:12,270
I am, but I don't wanna show it.

59
00:02:18,130 --> 00:02:21,660
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

60
00:02:21,680 --> 00:02:25,940
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

61
00:02:27,960 --> 00:02:34,860
♫Every step we take has a meaning♫

62
00:02:34,880 --> 00:02:40,780
♫No path is ever meaningless♫

63
00:02:42,290 --> 00:02:48,610
♫As long as our hearts keep searching♫

64
00:02:49,380 --> 00:02:53,860
♫One day, we'll find
what we're yearning for♫

65
00:02:53,880 --> 00:02:57,510
♫Walking alone is fine,
but it's better when you're by my side♫

66
00:02:57,530 --> 00:03:01,100
♫It won't be lonely
when you're here to walk beside♫

67
00:03:01,120 --> 00:03:04,040
♫Like a love that waits, waits at the D Dorm♫

68
00:03:04,690 --> 00:03:07,150
♫Like a love that remains,
remains at the dorm♫

69
00:03:07,170 --> 00:03:14,050
♫Meaningful love and good things
await on every path♫

70
00:03:14,070 --> 00:03:21,250
♫It might not be a coincidence
that we get to meet♫

71
00:03:21,270 --> 00:03:28,450
♫There might be hidden meanings
on the path beneath our feet♫

72
00:03:28,470 --> 00:03:35,670
♫Perhaps the D Dorm
is what led me to meet you♫

73
00:03:35,700 --> 00:03:39,480
[The D Dorm]

74
00:03:39,500 --> 00:03:41,380
Hello, everyone.

75
00:03:41,400 --> 00:03:43,350
Today, I'm back at

76
00:03:43,920 --> 00:03:46,520
the D Dorm!

77
00:03:48,090 --> 00:03:51,040
[Dom, occupation: YouTuber]

78
00:03:51,240 --> 00:03:52,700
- Here he comes.
- Oh, look, a celebrity.

79
00:03:53,440 --> 00:03:54,140
Guard Dum,

80
00:03:54,160 --> 00:03:54,870
Handyman Daeng,

81
00:03:54,890 --> 00:03:55,510
where is he?

82
00:03:55,960 --> 00:03:56,910
Where is Grandma Gaysorn's relative?

83
00:03:57,280 --> 00:03:59,190
Mr. Dom is standing right there.

84
00:03:59,410 --> 00:04:02,050
When I returned to my old house
in Chiang Mai,

85
00:04:02,070 --> 00:04:04,360
I discovered something.

86
00:04:04,530 --> 00:04:05,660
Today's episode

87
00:04:05,680 --> 00:04:07,760
will be a special episode

88
00:04:07,780 --> 00:04:09,450
that focuses on

89
00:04:09,470 --> 00:04:11,890
my grandma's love life!

90
00:04:13,520 --> 00:04:15,040
That's right. This episode will...

91
00:04:15,060 --> 00:04:17,050
be about my grandma's

92
00:04:17,079 --> 00:04:19,070
first love.

93
00:04:19,240 --> 00:04:20,670
Will I be able to complete this mission?

94
00:04:20,690 --> 00:04:22,230
Stay tuned to find out.

95
00:04:22,250 --> 00:04:23,460
Ugh...

96
00:04:23,480 --> 00:04:24,760
he's a YouTuber.

97
00:04:24,880 --> 00:04:26,120
This is gonna be a headache.

98
00:04:26,500 --> 00:04:27,670
I'm sick of these camera addicts.

99
00:04:27,690 --> 00:04:28,670
Hang in there, okay?

100
00:04:29,170 --> 00:04:31,050
Hello, my name is Dom.

101
00:04:31,070 --> 00:04:32,530
Mr. Dobby, can you
say hi to the camera?

102
00:04:32,740 --> 00:04:33,790
Hello, I'm Dobby.

103
00:04:33,810 --> 00:04:34,780
I'm the owner of this dorm,

104
00:04:34,800 --> 00:04:36,270
and I currently work as a freelance host.

105
00:04:36,290 --> 00:04:37,390
Feel free to contact me at

106
00:04:37,409 --> 00:04:38,430
062-41...

107
00:04:38,450 --> 00:04:39,740
- Hey!
- Hey!

108
00:04:39,760 --> 00:04:41,360
You just can't stay away from a mic!

109
00:04:41,740 --> 00:04:43,300
Gotta seize the opportunity.

110
00:04:43,320 --> 00:04:44,020
Isn't this a bit much?

111
00:04:44,400 --> 00:04:45,470
Feel free to contact me.

112
00:04:45,980 --> 00:04:48,280
- Mr. Dom, so you're Grandma Gaysorn's relative.
- Yes.

113
00:04:48,310 --> 00:04:50,270
My grandpa's first love.

114
00:04:50,500 --> 00:04:52,140
Do you have anything to back that up?

115
00:04:52,159 --> 00:04:52,650
Like...

116
00:04:52,670 --> 00:04:53,700
Even a photo of her would do.

117
00:04:53,720 --> 00:04:54,770
- Yeah, yeah.
- Mm.

118
00:04:55,070 --> 00:04:56,270
A photograph...

119
00:04:56,570 --> 00:04:57,320
I'm afraid I don't have one.

120
00:04:57,340 --> 00:04:58,300
- What?
- Huh?

121
00:04:58,320 --> 00:04:58,670
What?

122
00:04:58,840 --> 00:05:00,680
Hey, if you don't even have her photo,

123
00:05:00,700 --> 00:05:02,480
how am I supposed to believe you?

124
00:05:02,500 --> 00:05:03,880
- Yeah, that's right.
- Mm.

125
00:05:04,200 --> 00:05:05,870
I have other proof, though.

126
00:05:06,180 --> 00:05:06,800
Oh?

127
00:05:11,700 --> 00:05:12,290
Here.

128
00:05:12,330 --> 00:05:13,060
- Whoa.
- Huh?

129
00:05:13,980 --> 00:05:15,140
- Uh...
- Um...

130
00:05:15,160 --> 00:05:16,140
I'm sorry.

131
00:05:16,340 --> 00:05:17,280
You mean this tissue box?

132
00:05:17,300 --> 00:05:17,870
No,

133
00:05:18,890 --> 00:05:20,680
I brought this out for everyone to see.

134
00:05:20,900 --> 00:05:23,520
Because once you see what I’ve prepared,

135
00:05:23,700 --> 00:05:24,750
I guarantee

136
00:05:24,770 --> 00:05:26,940
you'll cry your eyes out.

137
00:05:28,140 --> 00:05:29,870
Here it is, T-REX tissue!
[They have great chemistry, though]

138
00:05:30,090 --> 00:05:31,050
Thick, tough,

139
00:05:31,070 --> 00:05:33,830
and soft like a newborn dinosaur's butt.

140
00:05:33,850 --> 00:05:36,240
T-REX tissue, shoo, shoo, shoo...

141
00:05:36,520 --> 00:05:37,500
Ugh!

142
00:05:37,520 --> 00:05:38,990
Why are we in an ad break?

143
00:05:39,010 --> 00:05:39,940
Where is it?

144
00:05:39,960 --> 00:05:42,390
The proof you mentioned.
Just show us already.

145
00:05:42,409 --> 00:05:43,520
- Yeah.
- That's right!

146
00:05:43,720 --> 00:05:44,530
I have it here.

147
00:05:46,800 --> 00:05:47,650
This is the real thing.

148
00:05:49,409 --> 00:05:50,670
Ta-da!

149
00:05:50,690 --> 00:05:51,470
Huh?

150
00:05:57,680 --> 00:06:00,810
This is something my grandma kept.

151
00:06:02,060 --> 00:06:02,780
Exactly!

152
00:06:03,040 --> 00:06:06,480
I gave this photo to Gaysorn myself.

153
00:06:11,300 --> 00:06:12,700
Oh, is this Gramps when he was young?

154
00:06:12,720 --> 00:06:14,250
- Mm.
- Hey, he's pretty handsome.

155
00:06:14,270 --> 00:06:15,330
He looks like Monkan Kaenkoon.

156
00:06:17,840 --> 00:06:18,600
Huh?

157
00:06:18,810 --> 00:06:19,860
There's a poem, too.

158
00:06:20,500 --> 00:06:25,520
"Your smile is as sweet as honey.

159
00:06:27,340 --> 00:06:32,760
I am completely smitten.

160
00:06:33,810 --> 00:06:38,500
I lie on my bed with you in my mind.

161
00:06:38,930 --> 00:06:40,280
Oh, how will my weenie..."

162
00:06:40,300 --> 00:06:41,360
- Huh?!
- What?!

163
00:06:41,610 --> 00:06:42,640
What kind of poem is this?

164
00:06:42,760 --> 00:06:44,250
Did he really write that?

165
00:06:44,270 --> 00:06:45,330
[Oh, how will my dreamy love reach you?]

166
00:06:46,040 --> 00:06:46,980
Dreamy love!

167
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:49,070
- Yeah.
- Oh, I see...

168
00:06:49,420 --> 00:06:54,500
"Oh, how will my dreamy love reach you?"

169
00:06:56,130 --> 00:06:57,200
What a weirdo.

170
00:06:57,760 --> 00:06:58,670
Dreamy love, huh?

171
00:06:59,300 --> 00:07:01,500
That kind of expression
sounded cool back then,

172
00:07:01,520 --> 00:07:02,760
alright?

173
00:07:03,660 --> 00:07:05,690
Do you remember
your grandpa's handwriting?

174
00:07:05,870 --> 00:07:07,070
Because if not...

175
00:07:07,200 --> 00:07:09,240
Wait, you have more evidence?

176
00:07:09,850 --> 00:07:10,460
You can use this!

177
00:07:10,480 --> 00:07:12,500
Ginkgo candy from
the Qilin Pushing Veggie Cart brand.

178
00:07:12,520 --> 00:07:13,390
Nourish your brain

179
00:07:13,410 --> 00:07:14,880
and keep Alzheimer's at bay.

180
00:07:15,090 --> 00:07:15,880
Try the ginkgo candy

181
00:07:15,900 --> 00:07:20,050
from the Qilin Pushing Veggie Cart brand
now, now, now....

182
00:07:20,380 --> 00:07:22,060
This really is Gramps' handwriting.

183
00:07:22,080 --> 00:07:22,670
Hm?

184
00:07:22,920 --> 00:07:24,840
- I remember his handwriting.
- Yes, yes.

185
00:07:24,860 --> 00:07:26,250
It really is his handwriting!

186
00:07:26,270 --> 00:07:27,240
That's right!

187
00:07:29,140 --> 00:07:29,850
Mr. Dom.

188
00:07:29,870 --> 00:07:30,500
Yes?

189
00:07:31,810 --> 00:07:33,050
Is Grandma Gaysorn...

190
00:07:34,520 --> 00:07:35,690
still alive?

191
00:07:48,490 --> 00:07:49,050
She is.

192
00:07:49,070 --> 00:07:50,230
- Oh, yes!
- Wow!

193
00:07:54,650 --> 00:07:57,840
My grandmother has always
wanted to see her first love once more.

194
00:07:59,690 --> 00:08:02,100
Don't miss what happens next tomorrow.

195
00:08:02,120 --> 00:08:04,360
And don't forget to like,
share, and subscribe to...

196
00:08:04,380 --> 00:08:05,850
the 'DODOMDI' channel!

197
00:08:05,870 --> 00:08:07,680
That's it for today!

198
00:08:07,700 --> 00:08:08,660
Bye-bye.

199
00:08:08,680 --> 00:08:09,110
Bye-bye.

200
00:08:09,130 --> 00:08:10,460
- Everyone, say goodbye to the camera.
- Bye-bye.

201
00:08:10,480 --> 00:08:11,590
Please submarine.

202
00:08:11,610 --> 00:08:12,310
- Hey, subscribe.
- Subscribe.

203
00:08:12,330 --> 00:08:13,360
Subscribe.

204
00:08:13,490 --> 00:08:15,240
- I've never been a YouTuber before.
- Subscribe.

205
00:08:15,260 --> 00:08:16,470
- Subscribe.
- Alright,

206
00:08:16,490 --> 00:08:17,330
see you.

207
00:08:17,620 --> 00:08:20,640
You had better
prepare to burn me a new outfit.

208
00:08:20,660 --> 00:08:22,060
Make it a handsome one.

209
00:08:22,080 --> 00:08:25,490
I will finally get to see Gaysorn!

210
00:08:29,720 --> 00:08:31,240
Are you serious, Dolly?

211
00:08:31,450 --> 00:08:33,539
You mean Dawin has fewer clients

212
00:08:33,620 --> 00:08:35,400
because people are turning to AI instead?

213
00:08:35,640 --> 00:08:36,600
Will it even be accurate, dear?

214
00:08:36,730 --> 00:08:38,400
Do you remember Pha
from the film set?

215
00:08:38,419 --> 00:08:38,970
Mm.

216
00:08:39,299 --> 00:08:41,330
The AI predicted that
Pha would be stabbed in the back.

217
00:08:41,610 --> 00:08:43,590
They found it as soon as they got home.

218
00:08:43,610 --> 00:08:44,390
Their hubby cheated on them?

219
00:08:44,410 --> 00:08:45,320
Someone broke into their house!

220
00:08:46,260 --> 00:08:47,650
Pha was stabbed in the back.

221
00:08:47,870 --> 00:08:48,890
They needed five stitches.

222
00:08:49,070 --> 00:08:49,600
Really?

223
00:08:49,620 --> 00:08:50,500
Nonsense!

224
00:08:50,940 --> 00:08:53,850
How can AI replace humans
in the art of spiritual divination?

225
00:08:53,870 --> 00:08:54,410
You don't believe me?

226
00:08:54,840 --> 00:08:55,610
I'll show you.

227
00:08:57,280 --> 00:09:00,490
Can you see if Dawin
will have any clients today?

228
00:09:01,580 --> 00:09:03,570
Mr. Dawin,

229
00:09:03,610 --> 00:09:05,740
your career luck is up and down today.

230
00:09:05,760 --> 00:09:08,610
Watch out for meat-related accidents.

231
00:09:09,650 --> 00:09:10,690
Isn't it fleet-related?

232
00:09:10,880 --> 00:09:11,870
Can't even get the words right.

233
00:09:12,500 --> 00:09:13,640
How can it be accurate?

234
00:09:17,580 --> 00:09:18,480
If what it said was true...

235
00:09:18,940 --> 00:09:20,250
- Oh, hey, hey.
- Whoa, whoa.

236
00:09:20,270 --> 00:09:21,070
Dolly... Dolly!

237
00:09:21,090 --> 00:09:22,830
- Go, go.
- Whoa. What, Mom? What?

238
00:09:22,850 --> 00:09:23,620
Is he choking?

239
00:09:23,640 --> 00:09:24,650
- Is he?
- He's choking.

240
00:09:27,600 --> 00:09:28,140
Oh!

241
00:09:28,670 --> 00:09:30,500
- It really is a meat accident!
- Dawin... Dawin!

242
00:09:30,960 --> 00:09:31,870
Are you okay?

243
00:09:31,890 --> 00:09:32,950
Just you wait,

244
00:09:32,970 --> 00:09:34,670
you're finished as a fortune teller, Dawin.

245
00:09:35,540 --> 00:09:36,200
Whoa...

246
00:09:36,220 --> 00:09:37,470
Then let's see

247
00:09:37,490 --> 00:09:39,680
who's more accurate, the AI or me.

248
00:09:39,700 --> 00:09:40,240
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

249
00:09:40,260 --> 00:09:41,870
- Oh, alright.
- Dolly!

250
00:09:42,100 --> 00:09:43,050
- Do we have to do this?
- Go on.

251
00:09:43,070 --> 00:09:44,100
Pick one card.

252
00:09:44,490 --> 00:09:45,140
Hurry!

253
00:09:45,160 --> 00:09:46,020
Choose wisely, dear.

254
00:09:48,290 --> 00:09:50,050
Be careful around high places these days.

255
00:09:50,380 --> 00:09:51,730
It could be fatal!

256
00:09:51,910 --> 00:09:53,530
Hey, Mom...

257
00:09:54,800 --> 00:09:56,490
How high are you talking about?
Chair-level?

258
00:09:56,690 --> 00:09:57,450
Higher.

259
00:09:57,470 --> 00:09:58,200
Chair!

260
00:09:58,380 --> 00:09:59,140
Higher!

261
00:09:59,290 --> 00:10:00,000
Chair!

262
00:10:00,020 --> 00:10:00,700
Even higher!

263
00:10:00,720 --> 00:10:01,310
Chair!

264
00:10:01,330 --> 00:10:02,120
Even higher!

265
00:10:02,140 --> 00:10:03,210
- Chair!!
- Higher!!

266
00:10:03,240 --> 00:10:05,240
Ugh, dear...

267
00:10:05,260 --> 00:10:07,510
Stop messing with him.
He's feeling down

268
00:10:07,530 --> 00:10:08,620
because he feels insulted by AI.

269
00:10:08,640 --> 00:10:09,200
Mm.

270
00:10:09,220 --> 00:10:09,910
Just wait and see...

271
00:10:09,930 --> 00:10:10,670
Dolly!

272
00:10:11,530 --> 00:10:12,200
Hey...

273
00:10:12,620 --> 00:10:14,930
you got a medical checkup
and hid the results from me, huh?!

274
00:10:15,360 --> 00:10:17,380
Dollar, I wasn't hiding it.

275
00:10:17,400 --> 00:10:19,660
I just put it somewhere safe

276
00:10:19,930 --> 00:10:20,830
so you wouldn't see it.

277
00:10:20,850 --> 00:10:21,920
That's called hiding it.

278
00:10:22,080 --> 00:10:23,140
And look at these results.

279
00:10:23,160 --> 00:10:23,870
Your fat levels are high,

280
00:10:25,460 --> 00:10:26,270
your blood sugar is high...

281
00:10:26,290 --> 00:10:27,090
Whoa...

282
00:10:27,850 --> 00:10:28,670
and your cholesterol is high!

283
00:10:28,850 --> 00:10:29,870
See?!

284
00:10:30,250 --> 00:10:31,400
You'll die from these high numbers.

285
00:10:31,420 --> 00:10:33,150
- Hey, Mom...
- Mm.

286
00:10:33,170 --> 00:10:34,670
How could you let yourself go this far?

287
00:10:35,010 --> 00:10:36,520
Who's gonna help take care of Mom now?

288
00:10:36,540 --> 00:10:37,660
Whoa, hey!

289
00:10:37,680 --> 00:10:39,020
How can you put all this on me?

290
00:10:39,220 --> 00:10:41,320
Tell Mom to take better care of herself, too.

291
00:10:41,480 --> 00:10:42,140
Think before you speak.

292
00:10:42,300 --> 00:10:43,070
Look at her.

293
00:10:43,200 --> 00:10:44,270
She's short,

294
00:10:44,850 --> 00:10:45,470
her knees are bad,

295
00:10:46,420 --> 00:10:47,280
and her body's sagging.

296
00:10:47,580 --> 00:10:48,410
What good would that do?

297
00:10:48,460 --> 00:10:50,820
You should be grateful she
can still cook and isn't bedridden!

298
00:10:50,930 --> 00:10:52,180
- Whoa.
- Whoa, there.

299
00:10:52,200 --> 00:10:53,520
My dears,

300
00:10:53,650 --> 00:10:55,340
if you want to argue, go ahead.

301
00:10:55,960 --> 00:10:57,090
But why curse me?

302
00:10:57,470 --> 00:10:59,340
- Mom, I'm not cursing you.
- Oh?

303
00:10:59,360 --> 00:11:00,650
- I just want to push him
- Look at him.

304
00:11:00,680 --> 00:11:02,570
- to take better care of himself for your sake.
- Come on.

305
00:11:03,840 --> 00:11:04,670
Go,

306
00:11:04,820 --> 00:11:05,500
go get changed.

307
00:11:05,520 --> 00:11:06,480
I'm taking you to work out.

308
00:11:06,500 --> 00:11:06,880
Go!

309
00:11:06,900 --> 00:11:08,090
- Come on.
- No!

310
00:11:08,490 --> 00:11:10,480
- Come on, go get changed.
- I don't wanna be a muscle-obsessed

311
00:11:10,500 --> 00:11:12,480
- gym rat like him.
- Go get changed...

312
00:11:12,500 --> 00:11:13,340
- Oh.
- Whoa.

313
00:11:14,270 --> 00:11:15,000
- Ow!
- Dolly!

314
00:11:15,030 --> 00:11:16,200
- Ow!
- Dolly.

315
00:11:16,320 --> 00:11:17,430
Whoa, Dolly?!

316
00:11:17,450 --> 00:11:18,830
Mom... Mom...

317
00:11:18,850 --> 00:11:19,710
- Ow!
- Dolly!

318
00:11:19,730 --> 00:11:20,270
What?

319
00:11:20,480 --> 00:11:21,560
- Dolly!
- Mom!

320
00:11:21,580 --> 00:11:22,840
See? I told you.

321
00:11:22,860 --> 00:11:23,870
Be careful around high places.

322
00:11:23,980 --> 00:11:25,070
- Yay!
- Hey!

323
00:11:25,480 --> 00:11:26,630
Now isn't the time for that, is it?

324
00:11:26,650 --> 00:11:27,450
My son is hurt.

325
00:11:27,470 --> 00:11:28,500
- Go help him.
- Mom...

326
00:11:28,520 --> 00:11:29,480
- Dolly!
- Ow...

327
00:11:29,500 --> 00:11:30,040
Dolly!

328
00:11:30,060 --> 00:11:31,050
Dolly, Dolly!

329
00:11:31,070 --> 00:11:33,010
[The D Dorm]

330
00:11:33,470 --> 00:11:34,060
Ugh...

331
00:11:34,080 --> 00:11:35,670
- Ow, hey... What?
- Oops, sorry.

332
00:11:35,690 --> 00:11:36,270
My bad.

333
00:11:36,290 --> 00:11:37,580
- Do it properly.
- Alright, sorry.

334
00:11:37,600 --> 00:11:38,770
Take this seriously...

335
00:11:38,940 --> 00:11:40,140
Wait, can I ask you something?

336
00:11:40,160 --> 00:11:40,670
Yeah?

337
00:11:40,800 --> 00:11:42,820
Why does Grandma have to
live in a separate room?

338
00:11:42,840 --> 00:11:44,250
Can't she just sleep in
her grandson's room?

339
00:11:44,270 --> 00:11:46,020
Well, Mr. Dom requested this.

340
00:11:46,200 --> 00:11:46,980
Maybe the room

341
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:48,940
is too small for two people.

342
00:11:50,690 --> 00:11:51,910
Oh, can I ask you something?

343
00:11:51,930 --> 00:11:52,480
Hm?

344
00:11:52,500 --> 00:11:54,250
If Grandma moved in,

345
00:11:54,540 --> 00:11:55,690
what are we gonna do next?

346
00:11:55,920 --> 00:11:57,570
Did Gramps tell you anything
in your dreams?

347
00:11:58,820 --> 00:12:01,420
Ever since I burned new clothes for him,
he hasn't shown his face.

348
00:12:01,930 --> 00:12:02,480
Huh?!

349
00:12:02,500 --> 00:12:03,730
What do you mean by that?

350
00:12:05,180 --> 00:12:05,870
Oh...

351
00:12:06,040 --> 00:12:06,880
I mean...

352
00:12:07,250 --> 00:12:09,240
He hasn't been visiting me
in my dreams at all.

353
00:12:09,260 --> 00:12:11,260
- I see...
- Yeah.

354
00:12:14,380 --> 00:12:17,850
Though we had to go our separate ways,

355
00:12:17,870 --> 00:12:21,840
I remember your smile vividly to this day.

356
00:12:22,560 --> 00:12:27,660
Though fate and death had parted us,

357
00:12:27,680 --> 00:12:31,070
my love for you, my darling...

358
00:12:32,690 --> 00:12:34,170
never faded.

359
00:12:35,730 --> 00:12:36,460
So?

360
00:12:36,480 --> 00:12:37,520
Am I handsome?

361
00:12:39,280 --> 00:12:40,700
Has Gaysorn not arrived yet?

362
00:12:40,720 --> 00:12:43,820
Everyone, this is the room
where Grandma Gaysorn and I

363
00:12:43,840 --> 00:12:45,780
will be staying temporarily.

364
00:12:45,800 --> 00:12:47,140
Can you say hi to the camera?

365
00:12:47,160 --> 00:12:48,930
- Hello, hello.
- Hello.

366
00:12:49,070 --> 00:12:49,670
Oops...

367
00:12:49,690 --> 00:12:51,470
Where is Grandma Gaysorn?

368
00:12:51,620 --> 00:12:52,780
She's here with us.

369
00:12:53,130 --> 00:12:53,870
Where?

370
00:13:01,320 --> 00:13:03,830
Gaysorn!

371
00:13:10,860 --> 00:13:11,870
Gaysorn...

372
00:13:17,500 --> 00:13:19,050
Dobby, this is not Gaysorn.

373
00:13:19,070 --> 00:13:19,860
What?

374
00:13:21,690 --> 00:13:22,340
Uh...

375
00:13:22,360 --> 00:13:25,660
Are you sure this is Grandma Gaysorn?

376
00:13:25,680 --> 00:13:26,840
I sure am.

377
00:13:27,050 --> 00:13:29,870
This is the real Grandma Gaysorn,

378
00:13:29,980 --> 00:13:32,010
Gramps Danai's first love.

379
00:13:32,520 --> 00:13:34,160
Oh...

380
00:13:34,670 --> 00:13:36,850
After fifty years apart,

381
00:13:37,060 --> 00:13:38,920
Grandma...

382
00:13:38,940 --> 00:13:42,280
will finally get to see Gramps
in his own home.

383
00:13:42,620 --> 00:13:44,090
Gramps Danai,

384
00:13:44,530 --> 00:13:47,020
aren't you glad that
Grandma finally came home?

385
00:13:47,040 --> 00:13:48,260
Glad, my foot!

386
00:13:48,930 --> 00:13:50,610
Gaysorn looks nothing like this.

387
00:13:50,960 --> 00:13:52,800
Grandma might

388
00:13:52,820 --> 00:13:55,320
look a little different because...

389
00:13:55,650 --> 00:13:57,470
she was in an accident.

390
00:13:59,540 --> 00:14:02,050
Even though Grandma was in an accident,

391
00:14:02,740 --> 00:14:06,680
she never forgot about Gramps Danai,
not even for a single day.

392
00:14:06,820 --> 00:14:08,620
Because she eats
[Hawaiian shirt guy, what's his name?]

393
00:14:08,640 --> 00:14:10,650
ginkgo candies from the Qilin Pushing Veggie Cart brand.
[Grandma is so cute]

394
00:14:10,670 --> 00:14:12,920
Nourish your brain and keep Alzheimer's at bay.
[What's the surprise today?]

395
00:14:12,940 --> 00:14:14,980
Ginkgo candy from the Qilin Pushing
[Product details, please]

396
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:15,940
Veggie Cart brand, brand, brand...
[Reminds me of my grandma]

397
00:14:17,360 --> 00:14:18,180
Ugh.

398
00:14:18,410 --> 00:14:20,490
Stop talking about Grandma.
Let's get back to the Qilin.

399
00:14:21,940 --> 00:14:24,450
Stop talking about the Qilin.
Let's get back to Grandma.

400
00:14:24,470 --> 00:14:25,400
- Oh...
- Mm.

401
00:14:25,760 --> 00:14:26,250
Alright.

402
00:14:26,270 --> 00:14:27,310
A long time ago...

403
00:14:27,330 --> 00:14:27,940
Mm.

404
00:14:27,960 --> 00:14:31,310
Grandma missed Gramps terribly.

405
00:14:31,330 --> 00:14:35,360
One day, she mistook someone

406
00:14:35,380 --> 00:14:36,860
in a passing car for Gramps

407
00:14:37,200 --> 00:14:39,790
and ran into the road after him.

408
00:14:39,810 --> 00:14:41,700
A durian truck came speeding

409
00:14:41,720 --> 00:14:42,910
toward her at 140 kilometers per hour...

410
00:14:42,930 --> 00:14:43,960
It crashed into her?

411
00:14:44,100 --> 00:14:45,000
She waved it down to buy some.

412
00:14:45,020 --> 00:14:45,870
- Oh.
- What?

413
00:14:45,890 --> 00:14:46,900
But tragically,

414
00:14:47,290 --> 00:14:48,500
given the truck's speed,

415
00:14:48,680 --> 00:14:50,250
the durians in the back

416
00:14:50,270 --> 00:14:53,270
fell straight onto Grandma's face!

417
00:14:53,520 --> 00:14:54,680
- Ouch...
- Oh...

418
00:14:54,850 --> 00:14:57,200
She was paralyzed

419
00:14:57,600 --> 00:14:58,530
for the rest of her life.

420
00:14:58,670 --> 00:15:00,900
She can no longer move her limbs.

421
00:15:01,760 --> 00:15:03,910
Not only that, Grandma

422
00:15:03,930 --> 00:15:06,080
had to undergo reconstructive surgery

423
00:15:06,100 --> 00:15:08,860
more than ten times
to restore her facial structure.

424
00:15:08,880 --> 00:15:11,160
That's why she no longer
looks anything like she used to.

425
00:15:11,180 --> 00:15:13,070
Grandma! Grandma...

426
00:15:13,180 --> 00:15:14,820
Why is your life...

427
00:15:14,840 --> 00:15:17,570
so tragic, Gaysorn?

428
00:15:19,490 --> 00:15:20,270
Poor thing.

429
00:15:20,520 --> 00:15:21,040
Hey,

430
00:15:21,060 --> 00:15:22,910
isn't being paralyzed after

431
00:15:22,930 --> 00:15:25,120
getting hit in the face with a durian
a bit far-fetched?

432
00:15:25,520 --> 00:15:26,660
It isn't, Ms. Danis.

433
00:15:27,010 --> 00:15:28,180
I've heard that

434
00:15:28,480 --> 00:15:31,300
a chunk of poop this size
once fell from an airplane

435
00:15:31,410 --> 00:15:32,510
onto someone's head

436
00:15:32,530 --> 00:15:33,450
and nearly killed them.

437
00:15:33,470 --> 00:15:34,240
Huh?!

438
00:15:34,260 --> 00:15:35,870
Yes, you can't be too careful.

439
00:15:36,180 --> 00:15:37,880
The reason I brought her here

440
00:15:38,010 --> 00:15:40,060
isn't just to grant her wish,

441
00:15:40,300 --> 00:15:41,870
but also to ask for your help.

442
00:15:42,260 --> 00:15:43,070
Mr. Dobby.

443
00:15:43,240 --> 00:15:43,770
Huh?

444
00:15:44,140 --> 00:15:44,940
He wants your help?

445
00:15:45,170 --> 00:15:47,280
My family and I
had to mortgage our house and land

446
00:15:47,480 --> 00:15:49,740
to pay for Grandma's treatment.

447
00:15:49,760 --> 00:15:51,950
That's why my Grandma and I...

448
00:15:51,970 --> 00:15:53,850
are close to losing
the roof over our heads.

449
00:15:53,870 --> 00:15:55,070
Oh...

450
00:15:55,490 --> 00:15:56,940
Grandma is crying...

451
00:15:58,570 --> 00:15:59,940
She's sad...

452
00:16:01,330 --> 00:16:01,910
Use this...

453
00:16:01,930 --> 00:16:02,650
What are you doing?!

454
00:16:02,970 --> 00:16:03,920
I'm going to wipe away her tears.

455
00:16:04,100 --> 00:16:04,870
Stop right there.

456
00:16:04,890 --> 00:16:07,360
That scratchy tissue
is no good for my Grandma's tears.

457
00:16:08,270 --> 00:16:09,010
You have to use this.

458
00:16:09,680 --> 00:16:10,670
T-REX tissue!
[Anyone just got here?]

459
00:16:10,940 --> 00:16:13,050
It's thick, tough, and soft.
[Could you repeat that? Didn't catch it]

460
00:16:13,070 --> 00:16:14,730
Perfect for the delicate skin
around your eyes.
[He's so good at selling it]

461
00:16:15,050 --> 00:16:17,490
T-REX tissue, shoo, shoo, shoo...

462
00:16:19,580 --> 00:16:20,420
[Ordered it]

463
00:16:20,440 --> 00:16:22,130
Here, let me wipe it for you.
[Grandma is so cute]

464
00:16:22,160 --> 00:16:22,540
[I ordered it]

465
00:16:23,520 --> 00:16:24,480
Is the tissue scratchy, though?

466
00:16:24,500 --> 00:16:25,860
I understand that...

467
00:16:26,270 --> 00:16:28,070
no one likes it when I do product tie-ins.

468
00:16:28,520 --> 00:16:29,240
But...

469
00:16:29,690 --> 00:16:30,800
if I don't do this,

470
00:16:31,530 --> 00:16:32,770
my grandma and I...

471
00:16:33,170 --> 00:16:34,630
won't be able to make ends meet.

472
00:16:36,260 --> 00:16:37,440
Dobby...

473
00:16:37,690 --> 00:16:39,210
help her.

474
00:16:40,520 --> 00:16:41,200
Mr. Dom,

475
00:16:42,010 --> 00:16:42,660
how...

476
00:16:43,290 --> 00:16:44,530
can I help you?

477
00:16:47,870 --> 00:16:48,660
Five million baht.

478
00:16:48,920 --> 00:16:49,890
- Huh?!
- Huh?!

479
00:16:50,270 --> 00:16:51,090
Five million?

480
00:16:52,540 --> 00:16:54,150
We need the money to pay off our debts

481
00:16:54,170 --> 00:16:55,840
and get our house back.

482
00:16:55,940 --> 00:16:56,970
My grandma and I

483
00:16:57,470 --> 00:16:58,670
need five million baht.

484
00:16:59,140 --> 00:17:00,300
- Five million...
- Whoa...

485
00:17:06,520 --> 00:17:07,970
Do you feel better
now that you have a cast on, dear?

486
00:17:08,050 --> 00:17:09,470
I'm okay now, Mom.

487
00:17:11,540 --> 00:17:12,900
But I'm not okay.

488
00:17:13,490 --> 00:17:14,599
How much longer will you keep this up?

489
00:17:14,720 --> 00:17:16,329
You're here, put him down.

490
00:17:17,020 --> 00:17:18,099
I can't, Mom.

491
00:17:18,260 --> 00:17:20,869
The doctor said, I mustn't let him put

492
00:17:20,890 --> 00:17:22,720
any weight on his leg at all,
or he'll get hurt.

493
00:17:22,839 --> 00:17:25,410
So you let him ride on your back
like a dusky langur?

494
00:17:26,040 --> 00:17:27,099
Hey, Mom.

495
00:17:27,119 --> 00:17:28,060
He deserved it.

496
00:17:28,180 --> 00:17:30,260
He's the reason I got hurt.

497
00:17:30,280 --> 00:17:31,590
He has to pay!

498
00:17:31,610 --> 00:17:32,250
Mm...

499
00:17:32,270 --> 00:17:33,020
I want to pee.

500
00:17:33,040 --> 00:17:34,720
Take me to the toilet, Khan Kluay.

501
00:17:36,400 --> 00:17:37,070
Dolly...

502
00:17:37,490 --> 00:17:39,020
Khan Kluay and a dusky langur.

503
00:17:39,600 --> 00:17:40,870
Khan Kluay and a dusky langur.

504
00:17:40,890 --> 00:17:41,970
Mm, go, go.

505
00:17:43,730 --> 00:17:44,640
Here's your ice cream.

506
00:17:48,010 --> 00:17:49,680
That ice cream truck took off so fast.

507
00:17:50,050 --> 00:17:52,280
Was it trying to win
a MotoGP trophy or something?

508
00:17:53,280 --> 00:17:54,730
Dollar, are you tired?

509
00:17:55,960 --> 00:17:57,690
Can you go grab my charger for me?

510
00:17:59,120 --> 00:18:00,460
It's alright, I'll go get it myself.

511
00:18:00,480 --> 00:18:01,350
Just sit there.

512
00:18:01,370 --> 00:18:02,270
I'll get it for you.

513
00:18:02,620 --> 00:18:03,290
Your charger, right?

514
00:18:04,670 --> 00:18:05,380
Here...

515
00:18:06,130 --> 00:18:07,050
Okay, one sec.

516
00:18:07,070 --> 00:18:08,080
Ow...

517
00:18:12,460 --> 00:18:13,070
Anything else?

518
00:18:16,220 --> 00:18:17,010
I'll teach him a lesson.

519
00:18:20,270 --> 00:18:21,120
Is that all?

520
00:18:29,680 --> 00:18:31,070
Here's your shrimp fried rice.

521
00:18:31,890 --> 00:18:33,450
Wait, wait, wait, Dolly,

522
00:18:33,470 --> 00:18:35,220
I can make you shrimp fried rice.

523
00:18:35,240 --> 00:18:37,070
Why did you make him
buy it from somewhere else?

524
00:18:37,300 --> 00:18:38,480
Well, I'm bored of it.

525
00:18:38,680 --> 00:18:41,040
I wanted to switch things up a little.

526
00:18:41,460 --> 00:18:42,820
You're messing with your brother,

527
00:18:43,370 --> 00:18:44,760
aren't you?

528
00:18:45,640 --> 00:18:48,500
And you, you're spoiling him too much.

529
00:18:48,520 --> 00:18:49,700
It was my fault,

530
00:18:49,810 --> 00:18:51,160
so I have to take responsibility.

531
00:18:51,180 --> 00:18:52,490
So I won't owe him anything.

532
00:18:53,490 --> 00:18:54,440
I've taken time off work.

533
00:18:54,780 --> 00:18:56,940
From now on, I'll be your legs

534
00:18:57,660 --> 00:18:58,670
until you recover.

535
00:19:00,610 --> 00:19:02,270
Okay, Dollar.

536
00:19:03,610 --> 00:19:04,740
Who's calling me?

537
00:19:05,520 --> 00:19:06,400
Yes, Oeng?

538
00:19:07,930 --> 00:19:08,520
Oh,

539
00:19:08,960 --> 00:19:10,180
the cafe at the entrance of the alley?

540
00:19:10,200 --> 00:19:10,810
I'll go.

541
00:19:11,160 --> 00:19:12,260
I've never been there before.

542
00:19:12,730 --> 00:19:13,350
Yeah, yeah.

543
00:19:13,370 --> 00:19:14,510
- Hey, hey...
- Oh, oh?

544
00:19:14,530 --> 00:19:15,320
Hey, what are you doing?

545
00:19:15,600 --> 00:19:17,100
You're going to the cafe, aren't you?

546
00:19:17,120 --> 00:19:18,680
- No need.
- I already told you I'd be your legs.

547
00:19:18,700 --> 00:19:19,050
Come on.

548
00:19:19,070 --> 00:19:20,670
Hey, wait. Don't, don't.

549
00:19:20,690 --> 00:19:22,280
It's embarrassing.
There are too many people.

550
00:19:22,300 --> 00:19:23,380
My friends are there.

551
00:19:23,650 --> 00:19:25,050
Mom, tell him to stop.

552
00:19:25,070 --> 00:19:25,750
Mom...

553
00:19:25,770 --> 00:19:27,450
He's your legs, not mine.

554
00:19:27,470 --> 00:19:28,650
Tell him yourself.

555
00:19:28,670 --> 00:19:30,210
Mom!

556
00:19:35,910 --> 00:19:39,210
[The D Dorm]

557
00:19:42,520 --> 00:19:43,390
Ugh!

558
00:19:43,410 --> 00:19:44,890
There goes my image.

559
00:19:45,300 --> 00:19:46,410
Dollar was carrying me around

560
00:19:46,670 --> 00:19:48,670
like I was his pocket dog.

561
00:19:48,690 --> 00:19:50,270
I'm starting to regret this.

562
00:19:50,400 --> 00:19:51,980
I shouldn't have faked my injury.

563
00:19:52,240 --> 00:19:52,960
What?

564
00:19:53,410 --> 00:19:54,440
So it was all an act?

565
00:19:55,970 --> 00:19:56,940
You were faking your injury

566
00:19:56,960 --> 00:19:59,370
because you didn't want to
be forced to exercise?

567
00:20:01,770 --> 00:20:02,690
- Ugh!
- Whoa?!

568
00:20:02,900 --> 00:20:03,940
Why are you angry?

569
00:20:04,050 --> 00:20:04,980
I'm angry at myself

570
00:20:05,330 --> 00:20:06,660
for losing to AI.

571
00:20:06,680 --> 00:20:09,130
I really thought you were injured
after falling from a high place.

572
00:20:09,580 --> 00:20:10,300
Hey,

573
00:20:10,960 --> 00:20:13,130
you have to keep this a secret.

574
00:20:13,330 --> 00:20:15,020
Don't tell Dollar about this.

575
00:20:15,040 --> 00:20:16,140
- Dang it!
- Whoa!

576
00:20:16,160 --> 00:20:17,640
What?! Why are you angry again?!

577
00:20:17,660 --> 00:20:18,730
I'm angry at myself again.

578
00:20:18,850 --> 00:20:20,270
If I lost to AI...

579
00:20:20,620 --> 00:20:22,130
how am I supposed to make money?!

580
00:20:22,260 --> 00:20:24,840
Stop obsessing over AI
and start caring about other people.

581
00:20:28,340 --> 00:20:29,370
Yes, Pha?

582
00:20:29,960 --> 00:20:32,360
An ad shoot needs a stylist
urgently for tomorrow?

583
00:20:32,890 --> 00:20:34,260
Double pay?!

584
00:20:34,280 --> 00:20:35,850
Oh, of course I can go.

585
00:20:35,870 --> 00:20:38,330
I'm free tomorrow, so I'll go.

586
00:20:39,680 --> 00:20:40,490
Where are you going?

587
00:20:41,980 --> 00:20:42,920
How did you get here?

588
00:20:42,940 --> 00:20:44,270
Well, I'm your legs.

589
00:20:44,520 --> 00:20:46,170
Wherever you go, I go.

590
00:20:46,290 --> 00:20:47,960
By the way,
you're working tomorrow?

591
00:20:47,980 --> 00:20:48,790
How are you gonna get there?

592
00:20:48,810 --> 00:20:49,720
I can go.

593
00:20:50,100 --> 00:20:51,280
I asked Drip for help.

594
00:20:51,300 --> 00:20:52,840
He'll take care of me on set.

595
00:20:53,020 --> 00:20:53,870
Not just Drip.

596
00:20:54,580 --> 00:20:56,270
I'll help him out as well.

597
00:20:56,410 --> 00:20:56,930
Huh?!

598
00:20:58,220 --> 00:20:59,300
If you try to stop me,

599
00:20:59,760 --> 00:21:01,050
I'm gonna expose you.

600
00:21:01,070 --> 00:21:02,270
Oh, so that's how
you're gonna do it, huh?

601
00:21:02,640 --> 00:21:03,470
Mm, yes.

602
00:21:03,600 --> 00:21:04,670
You don't need to go.

603
00:21:04,780 --> 00:21:06,040
I already have a lot of people looking after me.

604
00:21:06,060 --> 00:21:06,650
No!

605
00:21:06,810 --> 00:21:08,010
I said I'm your legs,

606
00:21:08,410 --> 00:21:09,970
so I'm going, too.

607
00:21:12,760 --> 00:21:13,760
How sweet...

608
00:21:13,780 --> 00:21:15,290
I want to cut my leg off.

609
00:21:16,180 --> 00:21:17,360
I want to cut my leg off...

610
00:21:21,250 --> 00:21:24,230
Are you really gonna pay him
five million baht?

611
00:21:26,880 --> 00:21:28,430
If Gramps were still alive,

612
00:21:28,530 --> 00:21:30,500
he'd definitely help Grandma Gaysorn.

613
00:21:31,180 --> 00:21:32,270
What are you gonna do?

614
00:21:34,140 --> 00:21:34,920
I'm not paying him.

615
00:21:36,120 --> 00:21:37,920
Not until I see all of the medical bills.

616
00:21:39,520 --> 00:21:40,460
That way, I can be sure that

617
00:21:41,240 --> 00:21:42,720
he isn't trying to scam us.

618
00:21:48,700 --> 00:21:54,100
I want to repent of my sins.

619
00:21:54,120 --> 00:21:59,210
I want to be punched
in the chin, one, two, three.

620
00:21:59,760 --> 00:22:04,670
If I could turn back time,
I would be your guard

621
00:22:05,580 --> 00:22:10,480
and protect you, ooh-ooh.

622
00:22:10,500 --> 00:22:13,360
Ooh-ooh, ooh-ooh.

623
00:22:13,380 --> 00:22:14,060
Bam!

624
00:22:14,080 --> 00:22:14,520
Bam!

625
00:22:15,250 --> 00:22:16,210
What are you looking at?

626
00:22:16,330 --> 00:22:17,210
I am drunk, you see?

627
00:22:18,090 --> 00:22:18,920
Mr. Dobby,

628
00:22:19,770 --> 00:22:20,770
be real with me,

629
00:22:21,020 --> 00:22:22,450
do you even have five million baht?

630
00:22:23,120 --> 00:22:26,020
You might have to sell this dorm to pay him.

631
00:22:26,840 --> 00:22:29,500
But this dorm is Gramps' beloved place, too.

632
00:22:30,410 --> 00:22:32,480
You're not gonna sell it
just to pay them, right?

633
00:22:34,520 --> 00:22:35,680
I'm not going to sell it.

634
00:22:35,700 --> 00:22:36,900
I told you I'm not selling it.

635
00:22:37,070 --> 00:22:38,270
So I won't sell it.

636
00:22:38,450 --> 00:22:39,470
Liar!

637
00:22:40,560 --> 00:22:41,340
I am drunk,

638
00:22:41,360 --> 00:22:42,470
so I want to listen to the lyre.

639
00:22:42,490 --> 00:22:44,130
I was not insulting you.

640
00:22:45,170 --> 00:22:46,440
- Mr. Dobby.
- Hm?

641
00:22:46,460 --> 00:22:48,740
Mr. Dom is livestreaming
with his grandma again.

642
00:22:48,760 --> 00:22:49,680
What? Let me see.

643
00:22:49,810 --> 00:22:51,000
Grandma,

644
00:22:51,020 --> 00:22:52,280
this is our Gramps Danai.

645
00:22:53,320 --> 00:22:54,490
Oh, Grandma...

646
00:22:54,660 --> 00:22:57,280
It'd be nice if you got to meet him

647
00:22:57,300 --> 00:22:58,140
while he was still alive.

648
00:22:58,410 --> 00:23:00,720
He would've definitely helped you,

649
00:23:01,070 --> 00:23:03,890
unlike his grandson,
who's still hesitating, right?

650
00:23:06,570 --> 00:23:07,690
Dobby!

651
00:23:08,080 --> 00:23:09,680
You have to help Gaysorn.

652
00:23:09,700 --> 00:23:12,540
I do not want to be any more
wrong than I already am!

653
00:23:13,520 --> 00:23:14,740
Look at me.

654
00:23:14,940 --> 00:23:17,360
Why aren't you talking to me, Dobby?!

655
00:23:17,380 --> 00:23:18,610
Huh?!

656
00:23:21,100 --> 00:23:22,670
What a ridiculous ghost.

657
00:23:22,930 --> 00:23:24,250
I shouldn't have given him alcohol.

658
00:23:25,520 --> 00:23:26,550
It's alright,

659
00:23:26,800 --> 00:23:28,670
I'll protect you.

660
00:23:29,870 --> 00:23:30,840
Whoa, whoa.

661
00:23:31,070 --> 00:23:32,830
Just like this
Furious Betta Mosquito Repellent Cream,

662
00:23:32,850 --> 00:23:34,380
you betta use it
if you don't want to get bitten.

663
00:23:34,400 --> 00:23:36,240
Don't forget to buy this for yourself.

664
00:23:36,370 --> 00:23:37,480
He used to get fewer than
a thousand viewers.

665
00:23:37,500 --> 00:23:40,670
Since her incident,
his views have hit tens of thousands.

666
00:23:41,720 --> 00:23:42,550
It's only natural.

667
00:23:42,570 --> 00:23:45,450
People are more interested in
other people's business than their own.

668
00:23:45,470 --> 00:23:46,760
It's normal.

669
00:23:48,610 --> 00:23:49,990
Yes, we're at...

670
00:23:50,010 --> 00:23:52,290
the D Dorm where my grandma...

671
00:23:53,660 --> 00:23:54,890
Gaysorn...

672
00:23:55,370 --> 00:23:58,050
I'm right here, Gaysorn...

673
00:23:59,360 --> 00:24:01,980
Seeing you

674
00:24:02,490 --> 00:24:04,940
feels like meeting the one

675
00:24:05,330 --> 00:24:09,000
I have always yearned for.

676
00:24:09,240 --> 00:24:11,870
You are the woman of my dreams.

677
00:24:13,410 --> 00:24:16,860
I am such a genius at this.

678
00:24:16,880 --> 00:24:18,490
If I became a lyricist,

679
00:24:18,920 --> 00:24:20,780
I would shoot to fame.

680
00:24:21,740 --> 00:24:23,060
What a ridiculous ghost.

681
00:24:24,480 --> 00:24:25,070
Mr. Dom,

682
00:24:25,760 --> 00:24:26,760
may I have a moment?

683
00:24:27,180 --> 00:24:28,820
I'm still livestreaming, though.

684
00:24:28,840 --> 00:24:31,170
You wouldn't mind if we talk
while I livestream, right?

685
00:24:31,200 --> 00:24:31,900
Oh...

686
00:24:31,920 --> 00:24:32,800
- Alright.
- Say hello to the camera.

687
00:24:32,940 --> 00:24:34,060
- Uh, hello.
- Yes.

688
00:24:34,360 --> 00:24:35,170
Um...

689
00:24:35,640 --> 00:24:37,520
Grandma Gaysorn had surgery, right?

690
00:24:37,980 --> 00:24:39,840
Could I see the medical bills?

691
00:24:40,150 --> 00:24:41,610
You think I'm scamming you, don't you?

692
00:24:42,740 --> 00:24:44,840
I don't have those medical bills.

693
00:24:45,970 --> 00:24:47,870
Because I'm not here to ask you for money.

694
00:24:48,660 --> 00:24:50,270
All I ask for is your empathy.

695
00:24:51,470 --> 00:24:53,210
My grandma is in this state

696
00:24:53,600 --> 00:24:54,920
partly because your grandpa

697
00:24:56,270 --> 00:24:57,450
broke his promise

698
00:24:57,470 --> 00:24:59,340
and refused
to run away with her to Chiang Mai.

699
00:25:00,900 --> 00:25:01,870
Whoa...

700
00:25:01,890 --> 00:25:02,470
Ms. Danis,

701
00:25:02,490 --> 00:25:03,740
the people are against us.

702
00:25:03,760 --> 00:25:05,280
They're threatening to boycott
our dorm, too.

703
00:25:05,440 --> 00:25:06,130
What?

704
00:25:06,500 --> 00:25:07,190
Hey...

705
00:25:07,210 --> 00:25:09,730
He says we can take this to Judge Jammy.

706
00:25:12,520 --> 00:25:13,070
Hey,

707
00:25:13,260 --> 00:25:14,060
listen!

708
00:25:14,080 --> 00:25:16,650
Mr. Dobby isn't asking you because
he doesn't want to pay you.

709
00:25:16,670 --> 00:25:19,050
Five million baht is a lot.

710
00:25:19,070 --> 00:25:20,940
He wants proof.

711
00:25:21,300 --> 00:25:22,960
Proof that you paid, you know?

712
00:25:22,980 --> 00:25:24,210
If you don't have that with you,

713
00:25:24,560 --> 00:25:26,270
you can tell us the name
of the hospital you went to.

714
00:25:26,520 --> 00:25:28,050
We can try to figure it out ourselves.

715
00:25:28,170 --> 00:25:28,670
Yes...

716
00:25:28,960 --> 00:25:30,570
If you don't want to help, that's okay.

717
00:25:31,070 --> 00:25:32,810
I'll take Grandma back to Chiang Mai.

718
00:25:33,050 --> 00:25:35,480
She was abandoned by Grandpa once before.

719
00:25:36,020 --> 00:25:37,370
I guess being abandoned again

720
00:25:38,050 --> 00:25:39,010
wouldn't make much difference.

721
00:25:45,340 --> 00:25:46,120
Dobby.

722
00:25:46,380 --> 00:25:47,520
Gaysorn...

723
00:25:47,860 --> 00:25:48,830
She swatted a mosquito!

724
00:25:48,850 --> 00:25:50,250
She was moving.

725
00:25:50,270 --> 00:25:52,650
She is no longer paralyzed.

726
00:25:52,670 --> 00:25:55,070
She is not paralyzed anymore!

727
00:26:01,730 --> 00:26:02,480
Mr. Dom,

728
00:26:03,930 --> 00:26:05,130
you want five million baht, right?

729
00:26:05,660 --> 00:26:06,160
Yes.

730
00:26:06,180 --> 00:26:07,070
I'll pay you tomorrow.

731
00:26:07,260 --> 00:26:07,820
Huh?!

732
00:26:09,640 --> 00:26:10,980
Thank you so much

733
00:26:11,000 --> 00:26:13,450
for understanding our struggle.

734
00:26:13,480 --> 00:26:16,160
Just like Seal Life Insurance
understands Thai people's struggles.

735
00:26:16,180 --> 00:26:17,870
Insurance made easy.

736
00:26:18,000 --> 00:26:19,720
Let this be your safety net.

737
00:26:19,960 --> 00:26:22,650
Ung, ung, ung, ung, ung, ung...

738
00:26:25,010 --> 00:26:27,270
[The D Dorm]

739
00:26:30,320 --> 00:26:31,130
Whoa?!

740
00:26:31,630 --> 00:26:32,960
It's just like you said.

741
00:26:32,980 --> 00:26:33,970
They're lying to us.

742
00:26:33,990 --> 00:26:35,510
Ugh, these con artists.

743
00:26:35,690 --> 00:26:37,710
I'll curse them till they run to jail!

744
00:26:37,730 --> 00:26:38,590
- Hey, hey, calm down.
- Whoa.

745
00:26:38,610 --> 00:26:39,850
Ms. Danis, come back.

746
00:26:39,870 --> 00:26:40,660
What now?

747
00:26:40,680 --> 00:26:42,210
Take a sniff. It'll calm you down.

748
00:26:42,660 --> 00:26:43,080
Huh?

749
00:26:43,380 --> 00:26:45,010
An inhaler from Chicken Ben Dover.

750
00:26:45,310 --> 00:26:47,420
Justin Hale, you'll like it.

751
00:26:48,050 --> 00:26:49,060
Ugh!

752
00:26:49,080 --> 00:26:51,210
Copying Dom will only make me angrier.

753
00:26:51,870 --> 00:26:52,520
Give it to me!

754
00:26:52,540 --> 00:26:54,270
What were you thinking,
messing with an angry person?

755
00:26:54,420 --> 00:26:55,450
We don't know

756
00:26:56,200 --> 00:26:58,220
what else they lied about,

757
00:26:58,420 --> 00:27:02,300
but the fact that he has
something Grandpa gave to Grandma Gaysorn

758
00:27:02,850 --> 00:27:04,060
means that...

759
00:27:04,680 --> 00:27:06,490
they probably know Grandma Gaysorn.

760
00:27:06,930 --> 00:27:09,100
We have to get more information from them.

761
00:27:11,030 --> 00:27:12,250
What a bright idea.

762
00:27:13,310 --> 00:27:15,050
If we let Ms. Danis complain to them,

763
00:27:15,070 --> 00:27:16,660
she'll throw a whip in the works.

764
00:27:16,680 --> 00:27:17,470
- Huh?!
- Huh?!

765
00:27:17,580 --> 00:27:18,640
Throw a wronch in the wake.

766
00:27:18,660 --> 00:27:19,290
- Huh?!
- Huh?!

767
00:27:19,310 --> 00:27:20,390
Throw a wrench in the wuss.

768
00:27:20,410 --> 00:27:21,130
- Huh?!
- Huh?!

769
00:27:21,260 --> 00:27:22,660
Whatever I'm trying to throw,
it's not your concern.

770
00:27:22,680 --> 00:27:23,250
Ugh.

771
00:27:23,880 --> 00:27:24,820
Dobby,

772
00:27:25,550 --> 00:27:26,960
do not accuse her of those things yet.

773
00:27:26,980 --> 00:27:30,090
She might actually be Gaysorn.

774
00:27:30,110 --> 00:27:31,310
Perhaps...

775
00:27:31,610 --> 00:27:35,860
my poem stirred her neurons,

776
00:27:35,880 --> 00:27:40,510
so her body miraculously
recovered from paralysis.

777
00:27:41,610 --> 00:27:42,530
Mr. Dobby,

778
00:27:42,590 --> 00:27:45,110
how are we going to

779
00:27:45,480 --> 00:27:47,370
get information from them, though?

780
00:27:48,660 --> 00:27:49,510
Yeah...

781
00:27:50,070 --> 00:27:51,130
True.

782
00:27:51,480 --> 00:27:52,490
I have a plan.

783
00:27:53,880 --> 00:27:54,870
What plan?

784
00:28:00,020 --> 00:28:00,810
We're going to

785
00:28:01,870 --> 00:28:04,410
tear the masks off those two tomorrow.

786
00:28:17,040 --> 00:28:17,730
Mr. Drip.

787
00:28:18,170 --> 00:28:18,490
Yes?

788
00:28:18,510 --> 00:28:21,050
Can you grab the blood-red shirt for me?

789
00:28:21,070 --> 00:28:21,480
Yes.

790
00:28:23,250 --> 00:28:24,480
Blood-red...

791
00:28:25,250 --> 00:28:25,820
So...

792
00:28:25,980 --> 00:28:27,240
what exactly is the color of blood?

793
00:28:28,680 --> 00:28:30,910
Is it the same as the blood
in the noodles we eat?

794
00:28:31,080 --> 00:28:32,880
I don't know how to explain it either.

795
00:28:33,210 --> 00:28:33,890
It's alright.

796
00:28:34,030 --> 00:28:34,730
I'll grab it myself.

797
00:28:35,230 --> 00:28:35,880
Stop right there.

798
00:28:36,190 --> 00:28:37,080
Let me do it for you.

799
00:28:42,060 --> 00:28:42,490
Mm.

800
00:28:42,830 --> 00:28:43,510
It's this one, right?

801
00:28:50,850 --> 00:28:52,680
Mr. Drip, can you give me my water bottle?

802
00:28:52,790 --> 00:28:53,300
Okay.

803
00:28:53,530 --> 00:28:54,260
I'll grab it for you.

804
00:28:56,530 --> 00:28:57,270
Here.

805
00:29:03,990 --> 00:29:05,080
Alright, fetch.

806
00:29:05,330 --> 00:29:06,230
Right away.

807
00:29:06,720 --> 00:29:07,530
Hey!

808
00:29:07,820 --> 00:29:09,180
This isn't funny.

809
00:29:10,140 --> 00:29:12,290
I'm not trying to be funny.

810
00:29:12,590 --> 00:29:14,480
My leg just hurts. I'm still fine.

811
00:29:14,770 --> 00:29:15,940
Why did you have to follow me here?

812
00:29:16,140 --> 00:29:16,970
Just go home.

813
00:29:16,990 --> 00:29:17,880
No.

814
00:29:18,410 --> 00:29:21,170
Mom already lost Dad.
She can't lose you, too.

815
00:29:21,750 --> 00:29:22,520
For Mom's sake,

816
00:29:22,540 --> 00:29:25,270
I won't let anything happen to you again.

817
00:29:25,990 --> 00:29:27,260
Ugh...

818
00:29:27,350 --> 00:29:28,230
All done?

819
00:29:28,250 --> 00:29:29,170
Yes.

820
00:29:30,030 --> 00:29:31,400
It's uncomfortable.

821
00:29:36,890 --> 00:29:39,120
Accept the truth, then.

822
00:29:39,520 --> 00:29:40,570
Never.

823
00:29:46,430 --> 00:29:48,650
Ugh, it's so itchy...

824
00:29:50,070 --> 00:29:51,230
What should I do?

825
00:29:51,250 --> 00:29:52,680
I can't take my cast off here, either.

826
00:29:53,700 --> 00:29:54,750
Are you alright?

827
00:29:56,930 --> 00:29:57,810
What's wrong?

828
00:29:57,830 --> 00:29:58,780
What should I do?

829
00:29:59,700 --> 00:30:00,490
Dollar!

830
00:30:00,790 --> 00:30:02,060
I'm going to the toilet.

831
00:30:02,280 --> 00:30:02,830
Whoa, whoa.

832
00:30:03,070 --> 00:30:03,990
Get on my back.

833
00:30:05,230 --> 00:30:05,640
What?

834
00:30:05,660 --> 00:30:06,310
Come on.

835
00:30:08,830 --> 00:30:09,320
What?

836
00:30:09,340 --> 00:30:10,300
Why are you heavier than usual?

837
00:30:10,680 --> 00:30:12,510
Oh, it's probably because of the cast.

838
00:30:15,020 --> 00:30:15,480
Oh.

839
00:30:15,710 --> 00:30:16,190
Ugh!

840
00:30:16,350 --> 00:30:16,950
Ugh...

841
00:30:17,090 --> 00:30:17,510
Oh.

842
00:30:17,650 --> 00:30:18,370
I can't take this anymore.

843
00:30:19,540 --> 00:30:20,280
Ugh!

844
00:30:21,140 --> 00:30:21,850
Here

845
00:30:22,150 --> 00:30:23,150
is your check for five million baht.

846
00:30:23,780 --> 00:30:26,420
Hey, it's five million.
Are you sure this is alright?

847
00:30:26,610 --> 00:30:28,260
I already agreed to this.

848
00:30:32,220 --> 00:30:33,550
Thank you so much, Mr. Dobby.

849
00:30:33,610 --> 00:30:34,380
Wait.

850
00:30:34,530 --> 00:30:35,530
I'll definitely give it to you,

851
00:30:36,450 --> 00:30:37,590
but there's one condition.

852
00:30:37,630 --> 00:30:38,530
Condition...?

853
00:30:39,010 --> 00:30:40,900
Last night, Grandpa came into my dream.

854
00:30:41,150 --> 00:30:42,250
He wanted me

855
00:30:42,440 --> 00:30:43,790
to help treat Grandma Gaysorn

856
00:30:43,810 --> 00:30:46,090
so that she could walk again.

857
00:30:48,370 --> 00:30:50,280
But her doctor said that

858
00:30:50,620 --> 00:30:52,660
she won't be able to walk
anymore, though.

859
00:30:52,680 --> 00:30:54,170
Mr. Dom, you have to understand that

860
00:30:54,420 --> 00:30:55,450
those doctors are quacks.

861
00:30:55,830 --> 00:30:56,260
Huh?

862
00:30:56,280 --> 00:30:57,690
But the person I brought today

863
00:30:57,710 --> 00:30:59,250
is a miracle doctor.

864
00:30:59,590 --> 00:31:00,170
Huh?!

865
00:31:00,570 --> 00:31:01,560
Doctor Chen!

866
00:31:14,280 --> 00:31:15,160
- Hello, Doctor Chen.
- Hello.

867
00:31:15,180 --> 00:31:16,000
Hello.

868
00:31:16,020 --> 00:31:17,860
- Hello, Doctor Chen.
- Mm, hello.

869
00:31:17,880 --> 00:31:18,760
Would you like me to help?

870
00:31:18,780 --> 00:31:19,950
It is alright.

871
00:31:20,860 --> 00:31:21,710
This is

872
00:31:21,980 --> 00:31:22,680
Doctor Chen.

873
00:31:23,030 --> 00:31:25,910
He's an expert at treating paralysis.

874
00:31:26,070 --> 00:31:28,140
He just came down from a mountain.

875
00:31:28,270 --> 00:31:29,330
Lingshan Mountain?

876
00:31:29,350 --> 00:31:30,010
The Golden Mount.

877
00:31:30,930 --> 00:31:33,290
He's here to rent a balloon-dart booth
for this year's Loy Krathong.

878
00:31:33,660 --> 00:31:34,680
So it was the perfect opportunity

879
00:31:34,700 --> 00:31:36,210
to ask him for help.

880
00:31:36,910 --> 00:31:37,890
Doctor Chen,

881
00:31:38,280 --> 00:31:40,200
do you think Grandma Gaysorn

882
00:31:40,220 --> 00:31:41,100
can be treated?

883
00:31:41,290 --> 00:31:44,130
I will have to checker reflexes.

884
00:31:44,150 --> 00:31:45,650
Why checkers, though?

885
00:31:45,670 --> 00:31:46,660
Checker reflexes.

886
00:31:46,680 --> 00:31:48,680
Now is not the time for checkers.
Treat her first.

887
00:31:48,700 --> 00:31:50,260
Check-er reflexes.

888
00:31:50,280 --> 00:31:51,880
- Check her reflexes!
- Mm.

889
00:31:51,900 --> 00:31:53,880
Oh, let me find my things...

890
00:31:54,710 --> 00:31:55,490
Here.

891
00:31:55,630 --> 00:31:56,280
- Whoa.
- Whoa!

892
00:31:56,550 --> 00:31:58,100
Too small, too small.

893
00:31:59,880 --> 00:32:00,880
- Whoa?!
- Huh?!

894
00:32:00,900 --> 00:32:01,750
Mm.

895
00:32:01,770 --> 00:32:02,830
Still too small.

896
00:32:02,850 --> 00:32:03,280
Whoa...

897
00:32:03,300 --> 00:32:04,680
- Still too small.
- Too small?

898
00:32:05,740 --> 00:32:07,060
- Oh, whoa!
- Huh?!

899
00:32:07,080 --> 00:32:07,540
Mm.

900
00:32:07,700 --> 00:32:09,590
This is perfect.

901
00:32:09,610 --> 00:32:11,860
- It fits perfectly in my hand.
- Wow.

902
00:32:11,880 --> 00:32:12,570
Dobby,

903
00:32:12,590 --> 00:32:14,030
are you really going to do this?!

904
00:32:14,610 --> 00:32:16,680
Gaysorn, I cannot bear
to keep looking at this.

905
00:32:16,930 --> 00:32:17,880
I am leaving.

906
00:32:18,850 --> 00:32:20,130
Wait, stop.

907
00:32:20,280 --> 00:32:21,460
What are you going to do to my grandma?

908
00:32:21,480 --> 00:32:22,680
I will examine her.

909
00:32:23,710 --> 00:32:24,530
Mr. Dom,

910
00:32:24,950 --> 00:32:26,980
if you want that five million,

911
00:32:27,220 --> 00:32:28,970
you'll have to let Doctor Chen

912
00:32:29,000 --> 00:32:30,750
examine her.

913
00:32:30,860 --> 00:32:31,990
But don't worry,

914
00:32:32,140 --> 00:32:34,370
Dr. Chen is highly skilled.

915
00:32:34,630 --> 00:32:36,610
- He won't make any mistakes.
- Mm, do not worry.

916
00:32:36,630 --> 00:32:37,500
Be careful.

917
00:32:41,180 --> 00:32:42,310
Ow!

918
00:32:42,330 --> 00:32:43,860
Ow...

919
00:32:44,650 --> 00:32:45,790
I shouldn't have stood there...

920
00:32:45,810 --> 00:32:46,530
Handyman Daeng.

921
00:32:46,630 --> 00:32:49,210
That was an example

922
00:32:49,230 --> 00:32:51,790
to show you what a normal reflex is like.

923
00:32:51,810 --> 00:32:53,510
- Oh, a demonstration.
- I see.

924
00:32:54,010 --> 00:32:54,500
Alright, alright.

925
00:32:54,740 --> 00:32:56,740
Now it is your turn, Grandma.

926
00:32:56,940 --> 00:32:57,480
Oh...

927
00:32:58,030 --> 00:32:58,680
Mm.

928
00:33:00,610 --> 00:33:03,170
Her nerves might not
have been stimulated for a long time.

929
00:33:03,190 --> 00:33:05,660
I have to wake them up.

930
00:33:25,260 --> 00:33:25,990
- What?!
- Whoa, whoa!

931
00:33:26,010 --> 00:33:28,390
Grandma lifted her leg!
I saw it with my own eyes!

932
00:33:28,540 --> 00:33:29,060
Well...

933
00:33:29,180 --> 00:33:29,880
I was kicked.

934
00:33:30,050 --> 00:33:31,450
What a miracle.

935
00:33:32,130 --> 00:33:33,820
Grandma can finally move her leg again.

936
00:33:34,230 --> 00:33:36,550
Thank you so much, Doc,
for treating my grandma.

937
00:33:36,570 --> 00:33:38,620
But I'll take care of her after this.

938
00:33:38,940 --> 00:33:39,480
Thank you.

939
00:33:40,250 --> 00:33:40,940
Wait!

940
00:33:41,710 --> 00:33:43,500
Why are you in such a rush?

941
00:33:43,890 --> 00:33:47,530
Doctor Chen's treatment
isn't even done yet.

942
00:33:51,850 --> 00:33:52,480
I was kicked.

943
00:33:52,500 --> 00:33:54,260
Right in my face.

944
00:33:55,620 --> 00:33:58,970
Her nerves still work,

945
00:33:59,100 --> 00:34:01,080
but they need to be stimulated.

946
00:34:01,290 --> 00:34:02,850
Next,

947
00:34:02,870 --> 00:34:05,370
I will have her steamed with herbs

948
00:34:05,530 --> 00:34:07,690
to boost her circulation.

949
00:34:07,710 --> 00:34:08,540
Come, come.

950
00:34:09,030 --> 00:34:11,659
It's just herbal steam.
Nothing to worry about, right?

951
00:34:12,659 --> 00:34:13,489
Just a little longer, okay?

952
00:34:13,510 --> 00:34:15,850
But herbs may not be enough.

953
00:34:15,870 --> 00:34:18,520
We need some toksin.

954
00:34:18,540 --> 00:34:19,679
Oh, what should we talk about?

955
00:34:19,699 --> 00:34:20,449
Toksin.

956
00:34:20,469 --> 00:34:21,460
You're gonna do it now, right?

957
00:34:21,480 --> 00:34:22,370
Tok-sin.

958
00:34:22,550 --> 00:34:23,370
Oh, toxins!

959
00:34:23,389 --> 00:34:23,880
- Mm.
- Oh.

960
00:34:24,050 --> 00:34:24,949
- Whoa...
- Toxins.

961
00:34:24,969 --> 00:34:27,370
Handyman Daeng, are you ready?

962
00:34:27,400 --> 00:34:29,389
- Whoa!
- Whoa!

963
00:34:29,409 --> 00:34:31,080
- So scary.
- Oh, wow...

964
00:34:31,300 --> 00:34:33,480
Start with scorpions.

965
00:34:34,860 --> 00:34:38,060
Handyman Daeng, be careful.
They're huge.

966
00:34:38,510 --> 00:34:40,179
Then add in the toads.

967
00:34:40,330 --> 00:34:41,730
- Whoa, how many are there?
- Oh, wow!

968
00:34:41,750 --> 00:34:43,060
- Get it there.
- Pour them in.

969
00:34:43,080 --> 00:34:44,980
Put them all in there.

970
00:34:45,300 --> 00:34:46,920
Next, add in the centipedes.

971
00:34:46,940 --> 00:34:48,130
Add in the centipedes.

972
00:34:49,659 --> 00:34:51,650
- Put them all in there.
- Hey...

973
00:34:51,670 --> 00:34:52,530
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

974
00:34:52,550 --> 00:34:54,330
What are you trying to do to her?

975
00:34:54,350 --> 00:34:57,300
Are you treating my grandma
or turning her into a poison monster?

976
00:34:57,350 --> 00:34:58,470
If my grandma goes in there,

977
00:34:58,490 --> 00:34:59,200
she's gonna die.

978
00:34:59,220 --> 00:35:01,400
This is not fatal. It is just mild venom.

979
00:35:01,420 --> 00:35:03,210
- Mild venom.
- No need to worry.

980
00:35:03,230 --> 00:35:04,680
So, are you done?

981
00:35:04,860 --> 00:35:05,880
Huh?!

982
00:35:06,470 --> 00:35:07,530
I dropped the container!

983
00:35:07,670 --> 00:35:09,460
Oh no, you dropped it.

984
00:35:09,480 --> 00:35:10,240
Uh...

985
00:35:10,260 --> 00:35:11,010
I'll...

986
00:35:11,230 --> 00:35:12,150
use my hand...

987
00:35:12,510 --> 00:35:13,390
to pick it up.

988
00:35:13,620 --> 00:35:15,900
Are you sure that's a good idea?
Don't risk it.

989
00:35:21,100 --> 00:35:23,600
Ow, ow, ow!

990
00:35:24,630 --> 00:35:25,410
Handyman Daeng.

991
00:35:25,430 --> 00:35:26,710
Ow!

992
00:35:28,490 --> 00:35:30,300
Hey, what's wrong?!

993
00:35:31,310 --> 00:35:31,840
What?!

994
00:35:31,860 --> 00:35:33,950
He's foaming at the mouth.

995
00:35:33,970 --> 00:35:34,890
Handyman Daeng,

996
00:35:35,230 --> 00:35:37,060
you left us far too soon.

997
00:35:37,080 --> 00:35:38,360
Oh...

998
00:35:38,580 --> 00:35:41,020
It is normal for accidents to happen.

999
00:35:41,290 --> 00:35:42,790
They do not happen very often, anyway.

1000
00:35:42,810 --> 00:35:43,700
Dobby.

1001
00:35:43,720 --> 00:35:45,280
- Huh?
- Bring her in here.

1002
00:35:46,260 --> 00:35:46,680
Grandma.

1003
00:35:46,700 --> 00:35:47,980
- Mm.
- She'll finally be able to walk.

1004
00:35:48,010 --> 00:35:48,850
Excuse me, Mr. Dom.

1005
00:35:55,890 --> 00:35:56,280
What?

1006
00:35:56,470 --> 00:35:57,920
- Whoa!
- Oh, wow!

1007
00:35:57,940 --> 00:36:00,310
We've just started, but Grandma
has already regained her strength.

1008
00:36:01,730 --> 00:36:02,950
- Splendid.
- You can do this, Grandma.

1009
00:36:02,970 --> 00:36:04,100
How miraculous.

1010
00:36:04,500 --> 00:36:05,880
The treatment worked so well.

1011
00:36:07,790 --> 00:36:08,490
Let's go!

1012
00:36:10,110 --> 00:36:11,310
I give up!

1013
00:36:11,330 --> 00:36:13,480
Stop! No more of this!

1014
00:36:13,500 --> 00:36:14,500
Dom,

1015
00:36:14,620 --> 00:36:15,480
you get in there yourself!

1016
00:36:15,740 --> 00:36:17,540
I'm not doing this! I'm leaving!

1017
00:36:18,230 --> 00:36:19,330
Stop right there.

1018
00:36:19,350 --> 00:36:20,770
Where do you think you're going?

1019
00:36:21,010 --> 00:36:25,510
You're all better now, Grandma Gaysorn?

1020
00:36:25,530 --> 00:36:26,890
Dearie...

1021
00:36:28,230 --> 00:36:30,530
I'm not Grandma Gaysorn.

1022
00:36:31,690 --> 00:36:34,420
Dom brought me here.

1023
00:36:37,710 --> 00:36:38,280
Uh...

1024
00:36:39,530 --> 00:36:40,540
Huh?!

1025
00:36:40,680 --> 00:36:42,330
You're not Grandma Gaysorn?

1026
00:36:42,500 --> 00:36:43,730
Your name isn't Gaysorn?

1027
00:36:43,750 --> 00:36:46,370
You've been lying to me my whole life?

1028
00:36:46,930 --> 00:36:48,050
I'm sad.

1029
00:36:48,070 --> 00:36:49,530
I'm so sad.

1030
00:36:49,860 --> 00:36:51,330
Then...

1031
00:36:51,350 --> 00:36:53,210
let me go home and cry.

1032
00:36:53,880 --> 00:36:55,190
- Hey!
- Mr. Dom,

1033
00:36:55,210 --> 00:36:56,540
you can cry in there.

1034
00:36:57,350 --> 00:36:58,680
Get in there.

1035
00:37:00,450 --> 00:37:01,080
Huh?

1036
00:37:01,750 --> 00:37:02,910
So?

1037
00:37:06,140 --> 00:37:07,340
- They're fake?
- Mm.

1038
00:37:10,060 --> 00:37:11,300
Did you trick me?

1039
00:37:11,440 --> 00:37:13,060
We simply gave you a taste
of your own medicine.

1040
00:37:13,080 --> 00:37:13,790
That's right!

1041
00:37:13,930 --> 00:37:15,780
You fake grandson.

1042
00:37:21,300 --> 00:37:23,140
Ugh...

1043
00:37:23,600 --> 00:37:25,070
There are rashes everywhere.

1044
00:37:25,580 --> 00:37:27,460
Dolly!

1045
00:37:27,480 --> 00:37:28,490
- Ow!
- Ow!

1046
00:37:28,820 --> 00:37:29,860
- Ow!
- Ow, ow.

1047
00:37:29,880 --> 00:37:31,370
Ugh, Dawin!

1048
00:37:31,390 --> 00:37:32,340
What were you running from?

1049
00:37:32,430 --> 00:37:34,220
I read the assistant director's fortune.

1050
00:37:34,390 --> 00:37:36,500
They challenged me to see
who was more accurate, the AI or me.

1051
00:37:36,670 --> 00:37:37,250
And?

1052
00:37:37,280 --> 00:37:38,750
So I decided to show off a little

1053
00:37:39,130 --> 00:37:39,710
and said...

1054
00:37:40,250 --> 00:37:41,380
they're secretly having an affair.

1055
00:37:41,610 --> 00:37:44,280
But I didn't know their wife
was sitting nearby,

1056
00:37:44,750 --> 00:37:46,230
so they chased me out and kicked me.

1057
00:37:46,680 --> 00:37:48,530
Ugh, you deserved that.

1058
00:37:50,170 --> 00:37:51,140
Let's go back.

1059
00:37:51,740 --> 00:37:53,540
If we're gone too long,
Dollar might get suspicious.

1060
00:37:56,280 --> 00:37:57,180
What?!

1061
00:37:57,480 --> 00:37:58,490
My cast is gone!

1062
00:38:00,060 --> 00:38:00,530
Huh?

1063
00:38:00,950 --> 00:38:01,600
Oh, no!

1064
00:38:01,620 --> 00:38:03,220
Shoot, my cast fell into the water!

1065
00:38:03,440 --> 00:38:04,660
Hey, what should we do?

1066
00:38:04,680 --> 00:38:05,860
Swim to it.

1067
00:38:05,880 --> 00:38:07,060
Hey, are you crazy?

1068
00:38:07,080 --> 00:38:08,280
I'm not. Go.

1069
00:38:08,410 --> 00:38:09,190
Dolly.

1070
00:38:10,140 --> 00:38:11,510
Dolly, where are you?

1071
00:38:12,030 --> 00:38:12,910
- I'm screwed.
- Dolly!

1072
00:38:12,930 --> 00:38:15,090
Dawin, talk to Dollar for me.

1073
00:38:15,110 --> 00:38:15,870
Dolly.

1074
00:38:15,890 --> 00:38:17,310
Hey, Dolly!

1075
00:38:19,390 --> 00:38:20,780
Walk faster, wimpy boy.

1076
00:38:22,020 --> 00:38:22,690
Stop.

1077
00:38:24,170 --> 00:38:26,280
Auntie Duang calls me "crunchy boy,"

1078
00:38:26,670 --> 00:38:27,480
not "wimpy boy."

1079
00:38:27,690 --> 00:38:29,410
Well, I'm calling you "wimpy boy."

1080
00:38:29,610 --> 00:38:30,930
Why were you on my back?

1081
00:38:31,270 --> 00:38:32,470
I meant to help my little brother.

1082
00:38:33,290 --> 00:38:35,010
I carried you all this way,
thinking the cast was heavy.

1083
00:38:35,570 --> 00:38:36,530
I didn't want to ride on your back.

1084
00:38:40,310 --> 00:38:40,900
Dawin.

1085
00:38:41,140 --> 00:38:41,700
Hm?

1086
00:38:41,880 --> 00:38:42,790
Have you seen Dolly?

1087
00:38:43,850 --> 00:38:45,010
No, no, I'm completely alone.

1088
00:38:47,550 --> 00:38:48,530
That thing floating over there...

1089
00:38:48,890 --> 00:38:50,280
looks like Mr. Dolly's cast.

1090
00:38:51,480 --> 00:38:52,060
Dolly.

1091
00:38:52,540 --> 00:38:53,440
Is he drowning?

1092
00:38:53,460 --> 00:38:53,880
Huh?!

1093
00:38:54,860 --> 00:38:55,550
- Dolly!
- Whoa, whoa!

1094
00:38:55,570 --> 00:38:56,950
- No, don't go.
- Dolly!

1095
00:38:56,970 --> 00:38:58,170
- I'm not letting you go.
- Let me go!

1096
00:38:58,190 --> 00:38:59,230
- Dolly!
- No!

1097
00:38:59,250 --> 00:39:00,370
- I'm gonna go help Dolly.
- No.

1098
00:39:01,610 --> 00:39:03,150
Maybe Dolly didn't fall into the water.

1099
00:39:03,300 --> 00:39:04,860
Why is his cast in the pond, then?

1100
00:39:05,700 --> 00:39:06,690
I'll help him myself.

1101
00:39:06,820 --> 00:39:07,670
Don't!

1102
00:39:09,060 --> 00:39:10,680
They are leaping like frogs.

1103
00:39:11,050 --> 00:39:12,120
Dolly!

1104
00:39:12,140 --> 00:39:13,470
- Never!
- What should I do?

1105
00:39:13,490 --> 00:39:14,790
- You can't go!
- Dolly!

1106
00:39:20,280 --> 00:39:21,050
Dolly...

1107
00:39:21,260 --> 00:39:21,820
No.

1108
00:39:23,130 --> 00:39:23,730
Let me go.

1109
00:39:26,150 --> 00:39:27,750
- I can't hold on much longer!
- I'm gonna save my brother. Let go!

1110
00:39:27,770 --> 00:39:29,270
Dollar, I'm right here!

1111
00:39:32,060 --> 00:39:33,020
- Dolly!
- Dolly!

1112
00:39:37,690 --> 00:39:38,510
- Be careful, okay?
- Ow.

1113
00:39:41,300 --> 00:39:42,750
Are you alright, Dolly?

1114
00:39:43,080 --> 00:39:43,770
Let's go see a doctor.

1115
00:39:43,790 --> 00:39:45,480
Hey, it's okay.

1116
00:39:45,820 --> 00:39:47,010
I'm alright.

1117
00:39:47,380 --> 00:39:48,510
I just slipped and fell into the pond.

1118
00:39:48,690 --> 00:39:50,030
Why weren't you being more careful?

1119
00:39:50,700 --> 00:39:51,910
How did you even fall into the pond?

1120
00:39:53,010 --> 00:39:53,880
Mm...

1121
00:39:55,980 --> 00:39:58,090
I was trying to work out.

1122
00:39:58,380 --> 00:39:59,050
Huh?

1123
00:40:00,030 --> 00:40:02,810
I was sad that I hurt my leg.

1124
00:40:03,770 --> 00:40:04,450
Dollar,

1125
00:40:04,680 --> 00:40:07,700
I want to work out with you again.

1126
00:40:09,990 --> 00:40:12,730
But I guess I'm just unlucky
when it comes to working out.

1127
00:40:12,970 --> 00:40:16,490
I always get injured
every time I try to work out.

1128
00:40:17,850 --> 00:40:20,510
I'm so sad...

1129
00:40:22,290 --> 00:40:23,230
Don't tell me

1130
00:40:23,510 --> 00:40:25,080
him falling into the pond was...

1131
00:40:26,550 --> 00:40:27,850
It was all an act.

1132
00:40:29,500 --> 00:40:30,550
I see...

1133
00:40:35,620 --> 00:40:36,330
Okay,

1134
00:40:37,080 --> 00:40:38,930
I won't force you to work out anymore.

1135
00:40:39,830 --> 00:40:41,490
That way, you won't
get injured like this again.

1136
00:40:41,510 --> 00:40:42,750
Really?

1137
00:40:42,770 --> 00:40:43,680
Mm.

1138
00:40:44,270 --> 00:40:45,350
You promise?

1139
00:40:46,810 --> 00:40:47,490
I promise.

1140
00:40:48,110 --> 00:40:49,890
Thank you, Dollar.

1141
00:40:50,940 --> 00:40:53,050
Oh, I love you so much.

1142
00:41:01,730 --> 00:41:03,830
You fell into the pond earlier, right?

1143
00:41:03,970 --> 00:41:05,010
That's right.

1144
00:41:05,150 --> 00:41:06,930
Why do I smell chlorine instead of mud?

1145
00:41:11,620 --> 00:41:13,900
I got out of the water and washed myself.

1146
00:41:14,060 --> 00:41:15,260
And your leg is better now?

1147
00:41:15,730 --> 00:41:16,680
You can walk normally?

1148
00:41:17,060 --> 00:41:17,610
Oh...

1149
00:41:18,530 --> 00:41:20,260
It's probably because of the adrenaline.

1150
00:41:20,280 --> 00:41:21,690
Now that you mention it...

1151
00:41:21,890 --> 00:41:23,550
my leg hurts.

1152
00:41:24,300 --> 00:41:25,060
Dawin...

1153
00:41:25,080 --> 00:41:25,860
Wrong leg!

1154
00:41:26,130 --> 00:41:26,810
Huh?

1155
00:41:28,830 --> 00:41:29,500
Oops.

1156
00:41:30,230 --> 00:41:31,080
Uh...

1157
00:41:33,670 --> 00:41:34,930
Simply put,

1158
00:41:35,770 --> 00:41:37,410
I'm sorry!

1159
00:41:37,950 --> 00:41:39,270
Dolly...

1160
00:41:39,290 --> 00:41:41,400
- Now, now...
- You lied to me, huh?

1161
00:41:41,420 --> 00:41:43,060
- No, Dollar.
- I'm not gonna let this slide!

1162
00:41:43,080 --> 00:41:44,530
Where are you going? Come here.

1163
00:41:45,480 --> 00:41:47,270
We might need to fetch that cast.

1164
00:41:47,750 --> 00:41:49,390
He might really need it after this.

1165
00:41:50,670 --> 00:41:51,670
- Hey, Dollar!
- Where are you going?

1166
00:41:51,690 --> 00:41:53,000
- Dollar! Hey!
- Where do you think you're going?

1167
00:41:53,020 --> 00:41:53,860
Help me, help.

1168
00:41:53,880 --> 00:41:54,490
Where are you going?

1169
00:41:54,510 --> 00:41:55,630
I got you.

1170
00:41:55,650 --> 00:41:56,590
Hey, Dollar.

1171
00:41:56,610 --> 00:41:57,120
Stop running.

1172
00:41:57,140 --> 00:41:58,070
- Ow... Hey.
- Sit down.

1173
00:41:58,090 --> 00:41:59,000
Hold him down.

1174
00:41:59,020 --> 00:41:59,860
- Ow, ow.
- Don't let him leave.

1175
00:41:59,880 --> 00:42:00,710
Why did you do this, hm?

1176
00:42:00,730 --> 00:42:02,050
- I didn't mean to.
- How many times have you done this?

1177
00:42:04,020 --> 00:42:05,530
Dobby...

1178
00:42:05,990 --> 00:42:08,900
she actually is not Gaysorn?

1179
00:42:09,340 --> 00:42:11,330
My heart is shattered.

1180
00:42:12,090 --> 00:42:14,310
It is shattered!

1181
00:42:14,450 --> 00:42:15,330
Ugh!

1182
00:42:15,870 --> 00:42:16,680
It's annoying!

1183
00:42:17,700 --> 00:42:18,380
Huh?

1184
00:42:20,630 --> 00:42:21,790
Uh... I mean,

1185
00:42:22,180 --> 00:42:23,530
I'm annoyed by these two.

1186
00:42:24,010 --> 00:42:25,280
When are you going to tell me

1187
00:42:25,300 --> 00:42:26,530
where you got all of this from?

1188
00:42:27,740 --> 00:42:28,510
Listen.

1189
00:42:29,580 --> 00:42:30,500
Dom

1190
00:42:31,070 --> 00:42:33,470
hired me to act paralyzed for 5,000 baht.

1191
00:42:33,890 --> 00:42:35,880
He told me to impersonate
someone called Gaysorn.

1192
00:42:36,700 --> 00:42:38,940
But my real name is Pom.

1193
00:42:39,310 --> 00:42:42,350
Ask him about the rest.

1194
00:42:42,860 --> 00:42:43,650
I don't know.

1195
00:42:43,670 --> 00:42:45,480
Dunno, dunno, dunno...

1196
00:42:45,650 --> 00:42:46,300
Dunno, dunno...

1197
00:42:46,320 --> 00:42:47,430
Wow, she fell asleep.

1198
00:42:49,390 --> 00:42:50,030
Hey.

1199
00:42:51,450 --> 00:42:52,950
If you don't want us to press charges,

1200
00:42:53,180 --> 00:42:54,350
tell us the truth.

1201
00:42:54,860 --> 00:42:57,170
So, you do know
the real Grandma Gaysorn, right?

1202
00:42:57,370 --> 00:42:59,390
I can't say that I do.

1203
00:42:59,850 --> 00:43:02,920
These keepsakes
were left behind by the tenant

1204
00:43:03,070 --> 00:43:04,520
who lived in my mom's house
fifty years ago.

1205
00:43:04,540 --> 00:43:05,510
- Huh?
- Huh?

1206
00:43:05,880 --> 00:43:07,790
Do you know where she lives now?

1207
00:43:07,810 --> 00:43:08,280
Yeah.

1208
00:43:08,710 --> 00:43:10,170
My mom told me that...

1209
00:43:11,140 --> 00:43:12,320
she lived there for a few years

1210
00:43:12,340 --> 00:43:14,260
before going back to Bangkok.

1211
00:43:14,280 --> 00:43:15,540
And she left these things behind.

1212
00:43:15,620 --> 00:43:16,930
I only found them recently,
while back on holiday

1213
00:43:16,950 --> 00:43:19,540
helping Mom clear out
and clean the rental house.

1214
00:43:21,780 --> 00:43:22,470
Oh.

1215
00:43:22,490 --> 00:43:24,270
She must have been heartbroken

1216
00:43:24,530 --> 00:43:26,070
because she left Gramps' love letter

1217
00:43:26,200 --> 00:43:28,290
and his photo behind.

1218
00:43:28,320 --> 00:43:29,170
True.

1219
00:43:30,300 --> 00:43:31,910
He promised to run away with her,

1220
00:43:32,520 --> 00:43:33,830
but he never showed up.

1221
00:43:34,330 --> 00:43:35,620
Who could blame her for leaving him?

1222
00:43:49,660 --> 00:43:50,940
Uh, but...

1223
00:43:51,340 --> 00:43:52,680
Since I came all this way

1224
00:43:52,950 --> 00:43:55,080
and even brought you Gramps' keepsake,

1225
00:43:55,530 --> 00:43:57,480
don't we deserve a little something?

1226
00:43:58,490 --> 00:44:00,170
It doesn't have to be five million baht.

1227
00:44:00,300 --> 00:44:01,350
5,000 would be enough.

1228
00:44:01,810 --> 00:44:03,480
I've got five fingers here.
Do you want them?

1229
00:44:04,150 --> 00:44:05,020
So fierce...

1230
00:44:05,340 --> 00:44:05,880
Hey,

1231
00:44:06,310 --> 00:44:09,100
aren't there any of Grandma Gaysorn's
photos at that house?

1232
00:44:13,080 --> 00:44:14,070
No.

1233
00:44:14,280 --> 00:44:14,930
Huh?

1234
00:44:15,250 --> 00:44:15,900
Well...

1235
00:44:16,980 --> 00:44:19,080
I already told you everything I know.

1236
00:44:19,870 --> 00:44:20,610
Now,

1237
00:44:20,820 --> 00:44:23,130
will you let Auntie Pom and me

1238
00:44:23,150 --> 00:44:24,300
go home already?

1239
00:44:31,390 --> 00:44:32,280
Then...

1240
00:44:32,780 --> 00:44:34,020
please excuse us.

1241
00:44:43,080 --> 00:44:43,830
Auntie Pom.

1242
00:44:44,170 --> 00:44:44,770
Auntie Pom!

1243
00:44:44,790 --> 00:44:45,710
Let's go.

1244
00:44:45,830 --> 00:44:46,990
They allowed us to leave.

1245
00:44:47,010 --> 00:44:48,190
Dunno... Dunno...

1246
00:44:48,210 --> 00:44:49,350
- Dunno... Dunno...
- Ugh.

1247
00:44:49,370 --> 00:44:50,570
- Ugh.
- Dunno...

1248
00:44:50,730 --> 00:44:51,990
Does she even know anything?

1249
00:44:55,630 --> 00:44:57,480
I rented this entire costume,

1250
00:44:57,710 --> 00:44:59,220
thinking we'd make some progress.

1251
00:45:00,620 --> 00:45:01,080
So,

1252
00:45:01,540 --> 00:45:02,520
what should we do next?

1253
00:45:02,660 --> 00:45:05,880
At the very least, we now know
Grandma Gaysorn moved to Bangkok.

1254
00:45:06,300 --> 00:45:09,480
She might be closer than we think.

1255
00:45:09,630 --> 00:45:10,220
Huh?

1256
00:45:11,700 --> 00:45:12,900
Perhaps she is...

1257
00:45:13,650 --> 00:45:14,740
- Huh?
- under the bed?

1258
00:45:18,370 --> 00:45:20,080
I wanted to lighten the mood,

1259
00:45:20,100 --> 00:45:21,480
so I cracked a joke.

1260
00:45:21,730 --> 00:45:22,660
Ugh...

1261
00:45:22,680 --> 00:45:25,080
I think this is just
stressing everyone out more.

1262
00:45:26,740 --> 00:45:28,010
Just kidding.

1263
00:45:28,680 --> 00:45:29,860
Would you like to borrow my watch?

1264
00:45:29,880 --> 00:45:31,060
Oh, it is alright.

1265
00:45:31,080 --> 00:45:32,510
I do not have the time.

1266
00:45:36,780 --> 00:45:39,140
[The D Dorm]

1267
00:45:39,970 --> 00:45:45,300
Oh, Danai, why is your life so tragic?

1268
00:45:45,860 --> 00:45:51,480
You found true love, yet failed to keep it.

1269
00:45:52,310 --> 00:45:58,010
You even made your daughter live in anguish.

1270
00:45:58,890 --> 00:46:01,790
You deserved it, old man.

1271
00:46:01,810 --> 00:46:03,210
Scritchy-scratchy.

1272
00:46:04,010 --> 00:46:04,680
Hey...

1273
00:46:06,620 --> 00:46:08,670
Why do you care, huh?

1274
00:46:08,850 --> 00:46:10,410
Just go wherever you want.

1275
00:46:11,020 --> 00:46:12,290
I want to be alone.

1276
00:46:12,590 --> 00:46:13,540
Grandpa,

1277
00:46:14,090 --> 00:46:15,330
what has gotten into you, huh?

1278
00:46:16,050 --> 00:46:17,880
I am trying to think.

1279
00:46:19,080 --> 00:46:22,980
All this time,
I have thought of nothing but Gaysorn.

1280
00:46:23,510 --> 00:46:24,370
I...

1281
00:46:25,580 --> 00:46:27,450
I want to apologize to her,

1282
00:46:27,740 --> 00:46:30,850
but I do not know if she...

1283
00:46:30,870 --> 00:46:34,120
even wants to hear it.

1284
00:46:36,170 --> 00:46:37,080
Oh, Grandpa.

1285
00:46:37,950 --> 00:46:39,480
You came all this way,

1286
00:46:39,900 --> 00:46:41,080
and now you're chickening out?

1287
00:46:42,230 --> 00:46:44,450
My mom and Grandma Gaysorn
are really not so different.

1288
00:46:46,470 --> 00:46:47,250
Stand tall,

1289
00:46:47,650 --> 00:46:48,900
then go apologize to her.

1290
00:46:50,100 --> 00:46:52,680
Whether you get yelled at again
or she forgives you,

1291
00:46:53,610 --> 00:46:54,930
it's better than doing nothing, Grandpa.

1292
00:47:00,180 --> 00:47:03,850
Oh, Dobby,
what a sweet grandson you are.

1293
00:47:03,870 --> 00:47:04,890
Stop it!

1294
00:47:06,350 --> 00:47:07,350
Your poems

1295
00:47:07,580 --> 00:47:08,930
are always a miss.

1296
00:47:09,290 --> 00:47:10,890
Was my great-grandfather
Shakespeare or something?

1297
00:47:11,630 --> 00:47:12,540
You just keep on composing.

1298
00:47:14,240 --> 00:47:14,850
There it is again.

1299
00:47:17,990 --> 00:47:18,860
Should I open the door for her?

1300
00:47:19,200 --> 00:47:20,240
Will I get hit in the head again?

1301
00:47:21,870 --> 00:47:22,530
Alright!

1302
00:47:23,880 --> 00:47:24,770
Ow!

1303
00:47:25,700 --> 00:47:26,130
Ouch...

1304
00:47:26,150 --> 00:47:27,790
Huh? You?

1305
00:47:27,980 --> 00:47:29,530
You banged your head on the door again.

1306
00:47:29,880 --> 00:47:31,750
- Do you...
- Is the door alright?

1307
00:47:31,770 --> 00:47:32,610
Ugh.

1308
00:47:32,630 --> 00:47:34,030
If it's gonna get me, it's gonna get me.

1309
00:47:34,050 --> 00:47:34,530
It hurts...

1310
00:47:34,680 --> 00:47:35,610
What do you want?

1311
00:47:35,630 --> 00:47:37,350
I have some good news for you.

1312
00:47:38,360 --> 00:47:41,500
Deang called to say he recovered
the footage from the day Gramps passed.

1313
00:47:42,050 --> 00:47:43,060
Now we'll know

1314
00:47:43,080 --> 00:47:45,590
who Grandma Gaysorn's relative is
in this dorm.

1315
00:47:53,880 --> 00:47:54,510
What's wrong?

1316
00:47:54,530 --> 00:47:56,260
You don't seem all that happy...

1317
00:47:56,280 --> 00:47:57,690
- Are you gonna cry?
- I'm glad. I really am.

1318
00:48:01,650 --> 00:48:02,650
Are you, though?

1319
00:48:03,260 --> 00:48:04,230
I am. I am.

1320
00:48:18,120 --> 00:48:18,850
Oh!

1321
00:48:18,940 --> 00:48:19,650
I remember now.

1322
00:48:19,670 --> 00:48:21,330
They live in Room 407.

1323
00:48:22,460 --> 00:48:23,650
Maybe no one's home.

1324
00:48:25,290 --> 00:48:26,650
There is not even a single photo.

1325
00:48:26,760 --> 00:48:28,290
How would I know

1326
00:48:28,310 --> 00:48:30,080
if they are related to Gaysorn?

1327
00:48:30,100 --> 00:48:31,370
Danis, have you seen the news?

1328
00:48:31,390 --> 00:48:33,440
Our dorm has a dismemberment case.
[Locals Terrified! Dismemberment Killer Still at Large]

1329
00:48:43,830 --> 00:48:47,270
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

1330
00:48:47,450 --> 00:48:51,170
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

1331
00:48:53,690 --> 00:48:59,170
♫Every step we take has a meaning♫

1332
00:49:00,920 --> 00:49:05,620
♫No path is ever meaningless♫

1333
00:49:08,100 --> 00:49:14,240
♫As long as our hearts keep searching♫

1334
00:49:15,150 --> 00:49:19,720
♫One day, we'll find
what we're yearning for♫

1335
00:49:19,740 --> 00:49:23,250
♫Walking alone is fine,
but it's better when you're by my side♫

1336
00:49:23,270 --> 00:49:26,850
♫It won't be lonely
when you're here to walk beside♫

1337
00:49:26,870 --> 00:49:30,390
♫Like a love that waits, waits at the D Dorm♫

1338
00:49:30,410 --> 00:49:32,760
♫Like a love that remains,
remains at the dorm♫

1339
00:49:32,790 --> 00:49:39,110
♫Meaningful love and good things
await on every path♫

1340
00:49:39,770 --> 00:49:46,500
♫It might not be a coincidence
that we get to meet♫

1341
00:49:46,980 --> 00:49:54,130
♫There might be hidden meanings
on the path beneath our feet♫

1342
00:49:54,150 --> 00:49:57,310
♫Perhaps the D Dorm
is what led me to meet you♫
